# PART 1: SCORING SYSTEMS CATALOG

## Bedside calculations

### Tier 1

**Anion gap** — Metabolic acidosis workup
> AG = Na - (Cl + HCO3); albumin-corrected AG = AG + 2.5*(4 - albumin)

**Corrected QT** — (see cardiovascular)
> QTc = QT/√RR (Bazett); QTc = QT/RR^(1/3) (Fridericia); QTc = QT + 0.154*(1-RR) (Hodges). RR = 60/HR. Normal <450ms (men), <460ms (women). Prolonged >500ms = high TdP risk.

**Corrected calcium** — Hyper/hypocalcemia assessment
> CorrCa = measured Ca + 0.8*(4 - albumin)

**Delta ratio** — High-AG acidosis with additional disorder
> Delta ratio = (AG - 12)/(24 - HCO3); <0.4 normal AG acidosis added, 0.4-0.8 mixed, >2 concomitant metabolic alkalosis

**MAP** — Perfusion pressure
> MAP = DBP + (SBP - DBP)/3

**Osmolal gap** — Toxic alcohol ingestion
> OG = measured Osm - calculated (2*Na + glucose/18 + BUN/2.8 [+ EtOH/4.6]); >10-15 abnormal

**Winter's formula** — Expected compensation in metabolic acidosis
> Expected PaCO2 = 1.5*HCO3 + 8 +/- 2

### Tier 2

**Base excess** — Acid-base status
> BE = (HCO3 - 24) + [0.14*(40 - PaCO2)? ] standard formula by blood gas analyzer

**Renal failure index / UOP** — (see renal)
> RFI = (Urine Na × Plasma Cr) / Urine Cr. >2 = intrinsic (ATN), <1 = prerenal. FENa = (UNa × PCr)/(PNa × UCr) × 100. <1% prerenal, >2% intrinsic. UOP: Oliguria <0.5 mL/kg/hr ≥6h. AKI (KDIGO): Stage 1: Cr ≥0.3mg/dL rise in 48h or 1.5-1.9x baseline; Stage 2: 2.0-2.9x; Stage 3: ≥3x or ≥4.0 or RRT.

**Serum osmolality** — Calculated osmolality
> 2*Na + glucose/18 + BUN/2.8

## Burns

### Tier 1

**Lund-Browder chart** — TBSA estimation (children)
> Age-specific body-region percentages

**Parkland formula** — Burn resuscitation fluids
> 4 mL LR x kg x %TBSA over 24h; half in first 8h from burn time

**Rule of nines** — TBSA estimation adults
> Head 9, each arm 9, chest 18, back 18, each leg 18, perineum 1 (adult)

**TBSA by palmar surface** — Rapid TBSA estimate
> Patient palm (with fingers) = 1% TBSA

## Cardiovascular

### Tier 1

**ASCVD Pooled Cohort Equations** — 10-yr atherosclerotic CVD risk (US guideline)
> 1-S0^exp(sum(beta_i*X_i - sum_mean)); age, sex, race, TC, HDL, SBP (+/- Rx), DM, smoking; coefficients in Goff et al 2013

**CCS class** — Angina severity
> I-IV by exertional threshold

**CHA2DS2-VASc** — Stroke risk in atrial fibrillation (guideline-mandated; most-validated AF score)
> CHF=1, HTN=1, Age>=75=2, DM=1, Stroke/TIA=2, Vascular disease=1, Age 65-74=1, Female=1; total 0-9. OAC if >=2 (men) / >=3 (women)

**EuroSCORE II** — Mortality after cardiac surgery
> logit = beta0 + sum(beta_i*X_i) over 18 variables (age, sex, Cr, LVEF, urgency, weight of intervention, etc.); online calculator required

**Framingham Risk Score** — 10-yr CHD/CVD risk
> Cox equation: S0(t)^exp(sum(beta_i*X_i - mean_i)); sex-specific coefficients for age, TC, HDL, SBP(+/-Rx), smoking, DM

**GRACE** — ACS mortality (in-hospital / 6-month)
> Points from age, HR, SBP, Cr, Killip, arrest, ST deviation, enzymes (0-372); low<=108, int 109-140, high>140. Risk = 1/(1+e^-(alpha+0.066*score)), alpha from published model

**HAS-BLED** — Major bleeding risk on OAC in AF
> HTN=1, Abnormal renal=1, Abnormal liver=1, Stroke history=1, Bleeding history=1, Labile INR=1, Age>65=1, Drugs/antiplatelets=1, Alcohol=1; total 0-9; >=3 = high risk

**HEART** — Chest pain triage in ED
> History 0-2 + ECG 0-2 + Age 0-2 + Risk factors 0-2 + Troponin 0-2; total 0-10; <=3 low, 4-6 moderate, >=7 high

**Killip class** — AMI severity
> I no HF=0, II rales/S3=1, III pulmonary edema=2, IV cardiogenic shock=3

**NYHA class** — HF functional class
> I no limitation=1, II slight limitation=2, III marked limitation=3, IV symptoms at rest=4

**QRISK3** — 10-yr CVD risk (UK)
> Cox model: age, ethnicity, smoking, BMI, BP, lipids, DM, CKD, AF, migraine, steroids, SLE, erectile dysfunction, severe mental illness, atypical antipsychotics, systemic corticosteroids, family history, Townsend score

**QTc (Bazett/Fridericia/Hodges/Framingham)** — ECG QT correction
> QTc = QT/sqrt(RR); QT/RR^(1/3); QT+1.75(HR-60); QT+0.154(1-RR)

**Revised Cardiac Risk Index (Lee)** — Perioperative cardiac risk
> High-risk surgery=1, IHD=1, HFrEF/HF=1, CVD=1, insulin DM=1, Cr>2=1; total 0-6; >=2 high risk

**STS risk score** — Mortality/morbidity after cardiac surgery (US)
> Bayesian logistic model of 40+ variables; STS calculator

**Shock Index** — Hemorrhage/shock screening
> SI = HR/SBP; MSI = HR/MAP; SI>0.9 abnormal, >1.3 high risk

**TIMI (UA/NSTEMI)** — Early risk in UA/NSTEMI
> Age>=65=1, >=3 CAD RF=1, prior CAD stenosis>=50%=1, ASA in 7d=1, severe angina 24h=1, ST shift>=0.5mm=1, troponin+=1; total 0-7

### Tier 2

**ABI / Rutherford / Fontaine / WIfI** — PAD severity
> ABI = highest ankle SBP / highest arm SBP; Rutherford 0-6; Fontaine I-IV; WIfI = wound/ischemia/foot infection grades

**ATRIA stroke** — AF stroke risk
> CHF=1, HTN=1, DM=1, Vascular disease=1, Age>=75=2? (weighting: age 65-74=2? published: age>75=2? ) components with published weights; total 0-13

**CHA2DS2-VA** — ESC variant (sex removed)
> CHA2DS2-VASc minus female sex; 0-8

**CHADS2** — Legacy AF stroke score
> CHF=1, HTN=1, Age>=75=1, DM=1, Stroke=2; total 0-6

**Duke Treadmill Score** — CAD prognosis from stress test
> DTS = exercise time(min) - 5*max ST deviation(mm) - 4*angina index(0 none,1 non-limiting,2 limiting); 0-?

**GARFIELD-AF** — AF stroke/mortality risk
> Registry-derived weighted model; includes age, BMI, BP, smoking, bleeding, alcohol, prior events

**ORBIT bleeding** — AF bleeding risk
> Age>=75=1, Reduced Hb/Hct=2, Bleeding history=2, Renal impairment=1, Antiplatelet use=1; total 0-7

**SAMe-TT2R2** — Warfarin vs NOAC decision in AF
> Sex female=1, Age<60=1, Minority race=1, interacting Drugs=1, Tobacco=2, >=2 comorbidities=2; total 0-8; >2 predicts poor TTR

**SYNTAX / SYNTAX II** — CAD complexity CABG vs PCI
> Angiographic: sum of weighted lesions (0-?); SYNTAX II adds clinical factors with logistic equation

### Tier 3

**CHARGE-AF** — Incident AF prediction
> Cox model: age, height, weight, SBP/DBP, smoking, antihypertensives, DM, HF, MI, stroke

**HATCH** — AF progression risk
> HTN=1, Age>75=2, TIA/stroke=2, COPD=1, HF=2; total 0-12

**Reynolds risk score** — Women's/Men's CVD risk
> Age, TC, HDL, SBP, smoker, hs-CRP, family history (DM for men)

## Coagulation

### Tier 1

**ISTH DIC score** — Overt DIC diagnosis
> Platelets >100=0, 50-100=1, <50=2; PT prolong <3s=0, 3-6s=1, >6s=2; D-dimer no rise=0, moderate=2, strong=3; fibrinogen >=1g/L=0, <1=1; total >=5 compatible with overt DIC

### Tier 2

**CRUSADE** — In-hospital bleeding post-ACS
> Admission Hct, CrCl, HR, SBP, sex, DM, CHF, prior VTE -> 0-100 score; >50 high

**JAAM DIC** — DIC (Japanese criteria)
> SIRS >=3 =1; platelets 80-120k or >30% drop=1, <80k or >50% drop=3; PT ratio >=1.2=1; FDP >=25 ug/mL=1, >=25 with strong=3; total >=4

**PRECISE-DAPT** — PCI bleeding risk (DAPT duration)
> Hemoglobin, WBC, age, CrCl, prior bleeding; points 0-25 via nomogram; >=25 high bleeding risk -> short DAPT

**SIC (sepsis-induced coagulopathy)** — DIC in sepsis
> Platelet 100-150=1, <100=2; PT-INR 1.2-1.4=1, >1.4=2; SOFA (resp/CNS) 1-2=1, 3-4=2? (liver/cardiovascular/renal) ; total 0-6; >=4 = SIC

**TIMI major/minor bleeding** — Bleeding definition in trials
> Hgb drop >=5 g/dL (major), >=3 with source etc.; TIMI criteria tables

### Tier 3

**ACUITY/HORIZONS bleeding** — PCI bleeding
> Age, female sex, Cr, WBC, anemia, STEMI/NSTEMI presentation; 0-50+

**ATRIA bleeding** — AF bleeding
> Anemia 3, severe renal disease 3, age>=75 2, prior hemorrhage 1, HTN 1; total 0-10

**HEMORR2HAGES** — AF bleeding (older)
> Hepatic/renal disease 1 each, Ethanol 1, Malignancy 1, Older>75 1, Reduced platelets 1, Rebleed risk 2, HTN uncontrolled 1, Anemia 1, Genetic factors 1, Excess fall risk 1, Stroke 1; total 0-12; >=4 high

## Critical care

### Tier 1

**APACHE II** — ICU mortality prediction
> 12 worst-first-24h physiologic vars x 0-4 (0-60) + age 0-6 + chronic health 0-5; total 0-71

**CAM-ICU** — ICU delirium diagnosis
> Acute change/fluctuation + inattention + (disorganized thinking OR altered LOC) = positive

**NEWS2** — Adult early warning (UK wards)
> RR (0-3) + SpO2 scale1/2 (0-3) + O2 supp (2) + SBP (0-3) + HR (0-3) + temp (0-3) + AVPU (0-3); total 0-20; >=5 trigger

**RASS** — ICU sedation scale
> +4 combative ... 0 alert ... -5 unarousable

**SAPS II** — ICU mortality
> 17 weighted variables summed (0-163); logistic mortality equation published (Le Gall 1993)

**SIRS** — Systemic inflammation (legacy sepsis screen)
> Temp>38 or <36=1, HR>90=1, RR>20 or PaCO2<32=1, WBC>12 or <4 or bands>10%=1; >=2 positive

**SOFA** — Organ dysfunction / sepsis severity (Sepsis-3)
> 6 organs x 0-4: PaO2/FiO2 (>=400, <400, <300, <200+vent, <100+vent); Platelets (>=150,<150,<100,<50,<20); Bilirubin mg/dL (<1.2,1.2-1.9,2-5.9,6-11.9,>=12); CV (MAP>=70, MAP<70, dop<=5/dobut, dop>5 or epi/nor<=0.1, dop>15 or epi/nor>0.1); GCS (15,13-14,10-12,6-9,<6); Cr mg/dL (<1.2,1.2-1.9,2-3.4,3.5-4.9/<500mL, >=5/<200mL); total 0-24

**qSOFA** — Screen for high-risk infection (outside ICU)
> SBP<=100=1, RR>=22=1, altered mentation=1; total 0-3

### Tier 2

**4AT** — Rapid delirium screen (geriatrics/ED)
> Alertness 0-4 + AMT4 0-4 + attention 0-2 + acute change 0-2; total 0-12; >=4 probable delirium

**APACHE IV** — ICU mortality (refined APACHE II)
> Acute physiology + age + chronic health + diagnosis; score 0-286 mapped to mortality

**CPOT** — ICU pain (non-verbal)
> Facial expression 0-2 + body movements 0-2 + muscle tension 0-2 + vocalization/intubated 0-2; total 0-8

**MEWS** — Early warning (legacy)
> RR+HR+SBP+temp+AVPU/mental, weighted 0-3 each; >=4/5 trigger

**OASIS** — ICU severity (claims/administrative use)
> 7 variables (age, GCS, HR, MAP, RR, Cr, LOS) weighted 0-48

**Phoenix criteria** — Pediatric sepsis (2024 Surviving Sepsis)
> Respiratory, cardiovascular, coagulation, neurologic dysfunction; 1 pt each component (age-adjusted); >=2 = Phoenix sepsis

**SOFA-based Sepsis-3** — Sepsis = infection + SOFA rise >=2
> Sepsis-3: infection + SOFA ≥2 from baseline. qSOFA: SBP ≤100 (1), RR ≥22 (1), altered mentation (1); ≥2 = sepsis. Septic shock = sepsis + vasopressors + lactate >2 despite fluids. SOFA: PaO2/FiO2, Platelets, Bilirubin, MAP/vasopressors, GCS, Creatinine (each 0-4). Total 0-24.

**Sedation-Agitation Scale** — ICU sedation
> 1-7 scale (unarousable to dangerous agitation)

### Tier 3

**LODS** — Logistic organ dysfunction
> Weighted 0-22 across 6 organs

**MPM II / MPM III** — ICU mortality at admission
> Logistic equation of 15/16 admission variables

## Emergency/General

### Tier 1

**Alvarado score** — Appendicitis
> Migration 1, anorexia/acetone 1, nausea/vomiting 1, RLQ tenderness 2, rebound 1, fever >=37.3 1, leukocytosis >10k 2, left shift >75% 1; total 0-10; >=7 probable

**Centor / McIsaac** — Strep pharyngitis
> Fever 1, no cough 1, tender anterior nodes 1, exudate 1, age 3-14 +1 / >=45 -1; total -1 to 5

**Sgarbossa (see surgery)** — 
> Sgarbossa (AMI + LBBB): Concordant ST elevation ≥1mm with positive QRS = 5 pts; Concordant ST depression ≥1mm in V1-V3 = 3 pts; Excessive discordant ST elevation ≥5mm or ≥25% of S-wave = 2 pts. ≥3 = AMI. Modified Sgarbossa (Smith): ST/S ratio ≥0.25 with negative QRS.

### Tier 2

**AIR score** — Appendicitis (refined)
> RIF pain 1, rebound 2, vomiting 1, WBC 10-14.9=1/>=15=2, neutrophils 70-84=1/>=85=2, CRP 10-49=1/>=50=2; total 0-12

**CIWA / COWS (see psychiatry)** — 
> CIWA-Ar: 10 items (0-7 each, orientation 0-4). Total 0-67. <10 mild, 10-18 moderate, >18 severe, ≥20 DT risk. COWS: 11 items (0-4/0-5). Total 0-48. 5-12 mild, 13-24 moderate, 25-36 mod-severe, ≥37 severe.

**EGSYS** — Cardiac syncope prediction
> Syncope during exertion 3, abnormal ECG 3? palpitations 4, dyspnea 2? ... ; >=3 predicts cardiac cause

**FeverPAIN** — Sore throat antibiotic guidance
> Fever 1, purulence 1, attend <3d 1, inflamed tonsils 1, no cough/coryza 1; total 0-5; 3-4 consider abx, 5-6 prescribe

**PERC / YEARS (see respiratory)** — 
> PERC: 8 negative criteria exclude PE: Age <50, HR <100, SpO2 >94%, No hemoptysis/estrogen/prior DVT-PE/unilateral swelling/recent surgery. YEARS: DVT signs, Hemoptysis, PE most likely. 0 items + D-dimer <1000 excluded; ≥1 items + D-dimer <500 excluded.

**RIPASA score** — Appendicitis (Asian populations)
> 12-14 items weighted (symptoms, signs, labs, sex, age); 0-16

**San Francisco Syncope Rule** — Serious causes of syncope
> CHESS: CHF hx, Hematocrit<30%, ECG abnormal, Shortness of breath, SBP<=90; any = high risk

### Tier 3

**Rosier (FAST) prehospital stroke screen** — Stroke recognition
> Facial droop, Arm weakness, Speech, Time + glucose/BP; >=1 = stroke code

## GI/Hepatology

### Tier 1

**BISAP** — Severe acute pancreatitis prognosis
> BUN>25=1, impaired mental status=1, SIRS>=2=1, age>60=1, pleural effusion=1; total 0-5

**CT Severity Index (CTSI)** — Pancreatitis severity on CT
> Pancreatic inflammation grade 0-4 + necrosis extent 0-6 (none 0, <30% 2, 30-50% 4, >50% 6); total 0-10

**Child-Pugh** — Cirrhosis severity / transplant listing, surgical risk
> Bilirubin <2/2-3/>3 =1/2/3; Albumin >3.5/2.8-3.5/<2.8 =1/2/3; INR <1.7/1.7-2.3/>2.3 =1/2/3; Ascites none/mild/mod-severe =1/2/3; Encephalopathy none/I-II/III-IV =1/2/3; total 5-15 (A 5-6, B 7-9, C 10-15)

**FIB-4** — Liver fibrosis (primary care)
> FIB-4 = (age * AST) / (platelets * sqrt(ALT)); <1.3 low, >2.67 advanced fibrosis (age-adjusted cutoffs)

**Forrest classification** — UGIB endoscopic stigmata
> Ia spurting, Ib oozing, IIa visible vessel, IIb clot, IIc flat spot, III clean base

**Glasgow-Blatchford Score** — Upper GI bleed risk stratification / safe discharge
> SBP 100-109=1, 90-99=2, <90=3; BUN 6.5-8=2, 8-10=3, 10-25=4, >=25=6; Hb men 12-13=1, 10-12=3, <10=6 (women 10-12=1, <10=6); pulse>=100=1; melena=1, syncope=2, hepatic disease=2, HF=2; total 0-23; 0-1 = very low risk

**MELD** — 3-month liver transplant waitlist mortality
> MELD = 3.78*ln(bilirubin) + 11.2*ln(INR) + 9.57*ln(Cr) + 6.43; floor bilirubin/INR/Cr at 1; Cr cap 4 (dialysis=4); max 40

**MELD-Na** — MELD with hyponatremia correction
> MELD-Na = MELD + 1.32*(137-Na) - 0.033*MELD*(137-Na); Na bounded 125-137

**SAAG** — Ascites cause
> SAAG = serum albumin - ascitic albumin; >=1.1 g/dL = portal hypertension

### Tier 2

**ALBI grade** — HCC liver function / prognosis
> ALBI = 0.66*log10(bilirubin umol/L) - 0.085*albumin(g/L); grade 1 <= -2.61, 2 > -2.61 to -1.39, 3 > -1.39

**APRI** — Fibrosis (HBV)
> APRI = [(AST/ULN)/platelet] * 100; <0.5 rule out, >1.5 significant fibrosis

**CDAI** — Crohn disease activity
> CDAI = SJC28? no: 8-item Crohn's: liquid stools x2 + abdominal pain x5 + general wellbeing x7 + opiates x30 + mass x10 + hematocrit deficit x6 + weight loss x1; 0-~600; <150 remission

**CLIF-C ACLF** — ACLF short-term mortality
> CLIF-C ACLF = 10*(0.33*CLIF-OF + 0.04*age + 0.63*ln(WBC) - 2)

**ELF test** — Advanced fibrosis blood panel
> ELF = -7.412 + 0.681*ln(HA) + 0.775*ln(PIIINP) + 0.494*ln(TIMP-1); >=9.8 advanced fibrosis? >=11.3 cirrhosis

**Glasgow Alcoholic Hepatitis Score** — AH severity
> Age, WBC, bilirubin, INR, urea each 1-2; total 0-12? (published: 0-12)

**Harvey-Bradshaw Index** — Crohn activity (simpler)
> General well-being 0-4 + abdominal pain 0-3 + diarrhea x2 + mass 0-3 + complications 1 each; 0-~20; <=4 remission

**Lille score** — Alcoholic hepatitis steroid response at day 7
> R = 3.19 - 0.101*age + 0.147*albumin + 0.0165*(bilirubin day7 - day0) - 0.206*(renal insufficiency) - 0.0065*bilirubin(day0) - 0.0096*PT; >0.45 non-responder -> stop steroids

**MELD 3.0** — US transplant listing (2023+)
> MELD3 = 1.33*(female) + 4.56*ln(bili) + 0.82*(137-Na) - 0.24*(137-Na)*ln(bili) + 9.09*ln(INR) + 11.14*ln(Cr) + 1.85*(3.5-alb) - 1.83*(3.5-alb)*ln(Cr) + 6; bounded inputs

**Maddrey Discriminant Function** — Alcoholic hepatitis severity
> DF = 4.6*(PT - control) + bilirubin(mg/dL); >32 severe (steroid candidacy with Lille)

**Mayo Clinic Score** — Ulcerative colitis activity
> Stool frequency 0-3 + rectal bleeding 0-3 + mucosal appearance 0-3 + physician rating 0-3; 0-12; <=2 remission

**NAFLD Fibrosis Score** — NAFLD advanced fibrosis
> NFS = -1.675 + 0.037*age + 0.094*BMI + 1.13*IFG/DM + 0.99*(AST/ALT) - 0.013*platelet - 0.66*albumin; <-1.455 low, >0.676 high

**Ranson criteria** — Pancreatitis severity (legacy)
> Admission: age>55, WBC>16k, glucose>200, LDH>350, AST>250 (each 1); 48h: Hct drop>10%, BUN rise>5, Ca<8, PaO2<60, base deficit>4, fluid sequestration>6L (each 1); total 0-11

**Rockall score** — UGIB mortality (post-endoscopy)
> Clinical: age <60/60-79/>=80 =0/1/2; shock none/HR>100/SBP<100 =0/1/2; comorbidity none/some/renal-liver-cancer =0/2/3. Endoscopy: dx 0-2; stigmata 0-2. Total 0-11

### Tier 3

**AIM65** — UGIB risk
> Albumin<30=1, INR>1.5=1, altered mentation=1, SBP<=90=1, age>65=1; total 0-5

**BARD score** — NAFLD fibrosis
> BMI>=28=1, AST/ALT>=0.8=2, DM=1; total 0-4; 2-4 at risk

**CLIP score** — HCC prognosis
> TNM points + Child-Pugh (1-3) + portal thrombosis (0-1) + AFP (0-1); 0-6

**Okuda** — HCC prognosis (legacy)
> Tumor size, albumin, bilirubin, ascites; stages I-III

