## Thrombolysis in Myocardial Infarction Risk Score for UA/NSTEMI (TIMI)

**Purpose:** Predicts 14-day risk of all-cause mortality, new or recurrent MI, or urgent revascularization in patients with unstable angina or NSTEMI.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Age ≥65 years | Patient age at presentation | boolean | Yes = 1; No = 0 | 1 |
| ≥3 CAD risk factors | Hypertension, hypercholesterolemia/dyslipidemia, diabetes, family history of premature CAD, current smoking | boolean | Yes = 1; No = 0 | 1 |
| Known CAD (stenosis ≥50%) | Previously documented coronary artery disease with ≥50% stenosis | boolean | Yes = 1; No = 0 | 1 |
| Aspirin use in prior 7 days | ASA taken within 7 days before presentation | boolean | Yes = 1; No = 0 | 1 |
| ≥2 anginal episodes in 24 hours | Two or more episodes of anginal pain within the 24 hours preceding presentation | boolean | Yes = 1; No = 0 | 1 |
| ST-segment deviation ≥0.5 mm | ST deviation (elevation or depression) of at least 0.5 mm on ECG | boolean | Yes = 1; No = 0 | 1 |
| Elevated cardiac biomarkers | Elevated troponin or CK-MB above local assay threshold | boolean | Yes = 1; No = 0 | 1 |

**Formula:** `TIMI = Sum of all 7 binary criteria (each 0 or 1)`

**Score Range:** 0–7

**Interpretation:**

- **0–1:** Low risk (~4.7% composite endpoint at 14 days)
- **2–3:** Intermediate risk (~8.3–13.2%)
- **4–7:** High risk (~19.9–40.9%)

**Reference:** Antman EM, Cohen M, Bernink PJLM, et al. The TIMI risk score for unstable angina/non-ST elevation MI: A method for prognostication and therapeutic decision making. JAMA. 2000;284(7):835-842. PMID: 10938172

**Limitations:** Originally derived from clinical trial populations (may underperform in real-world heterogeneous ED cohorts). Does not incorporate high-sensitivity troponin. Does not account for renal function or BNP. Subjective interpretation of 'risk factors' component.

