## Global Registry of Acute Coronary Events Score (GRACE)

**Purpose:** Estimates in-hospital and 6-month mortality in patients presenting with the full spectrum of ACS (UA, NSTEMI, and STEMI).

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Age | Age in years, with non-linear point assignment from nomogram | years | 0–100 years | 0–100 points (non-linear, assigned via lookup table/nomogram) |
| Heart rate | Heart rate at presentation (bpm), non-linear point assignment | bpm | 0–300 | 0–46 points (non-linear) |
| Systolic blood pressure | SBP at presentation (mmHg), non-linear point assignment | mmHg | 0–300 | 0–58 points (non-linear, inverse relationship) |
| Serum creatinine | Creatinine at presentation (mg/dL), non-linear point assignment | mg/dL | 0–4+ mg/dL | 0–28 points (non-linear) |
| Killip class | Clinical heart failure classification at presentation | categorical | I = no HF; II = rales/JVD/ S3; III = pulmonary edema; IV = cardiogenic shock | I = 0; II = 20; III = 39; IV = 59 |
| Cardiac arrest at admission | Whether patient had cardiac arrest at time of presentation | boolean | Yes/No | Yes = 39 |
| ST-segment deviation | ST deviation (elevation or depression) on presenting ECG | boolean | Yes/No | Yes = 28 |
| Elevated cardiac biomarkers | Elevated troponin or CK-MB | boolean | Yes/No | Yes = 14 |

**Formula:** `GRACE = Age_points + HR_points + SBP_points + Creatinine_points + Killip_points + Cardiac_arrest(39 if yes) + ST_deviation(28 if yes) + Elevated_biomarkers(14 if yes). Non-linear point assignments for continuous variables are derived from the published nomogram/lookup tables; the GRACE 2.0 web calculator uses polynomial regression: Risk = 1/(1 + e^(-(β₀ + β₁×age + β₂×HR + β₃×SBP + β₄×Cr + β₅×Killip + β₆×arrest + β₇×STdev + β₈×troponin))) with published coefficients. Verify exact polynomial coefficients from the GRACE 2.0 publication.`

**Score Range:** 0–372 (original); 1–372

**Interpretation:**

- **1–108:** Low risk: in-hospital mortality <1%; 6-month mortality <3%
- **109–140:** Intermediate risk: in-hospital mortality 1–3%; 6-month mortality 3–8%
- **141–372:** High risk: in-hospital mortality >3%; 6-month mortality >8%

**Reference:** Granger CB, Goldberg RJ, Dabbous O, et al. Predictors of hospital mortality in the Global Registry of Acute Coronary Events. Arch Intern Med. 2003;163(19):2345-2353. PMID: 14581255

**Limitations:** Non-linear point assignment requires lookup tables or web calculator (not easily computed at bedside). Requires serum creatinine. Less validated in specific subgroups (very elderly, CKD, racial/ethnic minorities in some studies). GRACE 2.0 preferred for use with calculator apps.

