## TIMI Risk Index (TRI)

**Purpose:** Simplified bedside risk index for 30-day mortality in STEMI using three readily available variables.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Age | Age in years | years | continuous | multiplier in formula |
| Heart rate | Heart rate at presentation in beats per minute | bpm | continuous | multiplier in formula |
| Systolic blood pressure | Systolic blood pressure at presentation in mmHg | mmHg | continuous | denominator in formula |

**Formula:** `TIMI Risk Index = (Heart_rate × Age / 10) / Systolic_BP`

**Score Range:** continuous (typically 0–100+)

**Interpretation:**

- **<12.5:** Low risk for 30-day mortality (~1%)
- **12.5–29.5:** Intermediate risk (~3–5%)
- **>29.5:** High risk (~10–15%)

**Reference:** Morrow DA, Antman EM, Giugliano RP, et al. A simple risk index for rapid initial triage of patients with ST-elevation myocardial infarction: an InTIME II substudy. Lancet. 2001;358(9293):1571-1575. PMID: 11716882

**Limitations:** Originally validated in STEMI only; less studied in NSTEMI/UA. Does not include troponin or ECG variables. Simplified — may miss nuanced risk captured by GRACE or full TIMI.

