## Sgarbossa Criteria

**Purpose:** Identifies acute myocardial infarction in patients with left bundle branch block (LBBB) on ECG.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Concordant ST elevation ≥1 mm | ST-segment elevation ≥1 mm in any lead with a positive QRS complex (concordant with QRS) | boolean | Yes/No | 5 |
| Concordant ST depression ≥1 mm in V1–V3 | ST depression ≥1 mm in V1, V2, or V3 (concordant with the negative QRS in these leads) | boolean | Yes/No | 3 |
| Discordant ST elevation ≥5 mm | ST elevation ≥5 mm in any lead with a negative QRS (discordant) | boolean | Yes/No | 2 |

**Formula:** `Sgarbossa = Concordant_ST_elevation(5 if yes) + Concordant_ST_depression_V1-V3(3 if yes) + Discordant_ST_elevation_≥5mm(2 if yes)`

**Score Range:** 0–10

**Interpretation:**

- **≥3:** High specificity (>90%) for acute MI. Recommended to activate cath lab.
- **<3:** Insufficient specificity to diagnose AMI in LBBB. Consider modified Sgarbossa.

**Reference:** Sgarbossa EB, Pinski SL, Barbagelata A, et al. Electrocardiographic diagnosis of evolving acute myocardial infarction in the presence of left bundle-branch block. N Engl J Med. 1996;334(8):481-487. PMID: 8559200

**Limitations:** High specificity but low sensitivity (~20–36%) for AMI. Discordant ST elevation criterion (≥5 mm) was the most weighted but least specific. Modified Sgarbossa (using ST/S ratio ≤-0.25 in discordant leads) improves sensitivity.

