## Modified Sgarbossa Criteria

**Purpose:** Improved sensitivity for diagnosing acute MI in LBBB by replacing the absolute discordant ST elevation threshold with an ST/S ratio criterion.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Concordant ST elevation ≥1 mm | ST elevation ≥1 mm in any lead with positive QRS | boolean | Yes/No | 5 |
| Concordant ST depression ≥1 mm in V1–V3 | ST depression ≥1 mm in V1, V2, or V3 | boolean | Yes/No | 3 |
| Proportionally excessive discordant ST elevation (ST/S ratio ≤ -0.25) | In any lead with negative QRS, ratio of ST elevation to S-wave depth ≤ -0.25 (i.e., ST elevation is ≥25% of the S-wave depth) | boolean | Yes/No | 2 |

**Formula:** `Modified Sgarbossa = Concordant_ST_elevation(5) + Concordant_ST_depression_V1-V3(3) + ST/S_ratio_≤-0.25(2)`

**Score Range:** 0–10

**Interpretation:**

- **≥3:** Positive for acute MI. High sensitivity (~80%) with maintained specificity (~90%).
- **<3:** Negative for acute MI criteria in LBBB.

**Reference:** Smith SW, Dodd KW, Henry TD, et al. Diagnosis of ST-elevation myocardial infarction in the presence of left bundle branch block with the ST-elevation to S-wave ratio in a modification of the Sgarbossa criteria. Ann Emerg Med. 2012;59(2):116-123. PMID: 21944788

**Limitations:** ST/S ratio can be difficult to measure when S-wave is very shallow. Requires careful measurement technique. Validation cohorts are relatively small. Not yet incorporated into all guidelines.

