## TIMI Risk Score for ST-Elevation Myocardial Infarction (TIMI-STEMI)

**Purpose:** Predicts 30-day mortality in patients with ST-elevation myocardial infarction to guide management.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Age 65–74 | Age between 65 and 74 years | boolean | Yes/No | 2 |
| Age ≥75 | Age 75 years or older | boolean | Yes/No | 3 |
| Diabetes mellitus or hypertension or angina | History of DM, HTN, or angina | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| SBP <100 mmHg | Systolic blood pressure less than 100 at presentation | boolean | Yes/No | 3 |
| Heart rate >100 bpm | Heart rate greater than 100 at presentation | boolean | Yes/No | 2 |
| Killip class II–IV | Signs of heart failure (Killip ≥2) | boolean | Yes/No | 2 |
| Anterior ST elevation or LBBB | Anterior STEMI or new/presumably new LBBB | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Time to treatment >4 hours | Symptom onset to treatment >4 hours | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Body weight <67 kg | Weight less than 67 kg | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |

**Formula:** `TIMI-STEMI = Age_65-74(2) + Age_≥75(3) + DM_or_HTN_or_angina(1) + SBP<100(3) + HR>100(2) + Killip_II-IV(2) + Anterior_or_LBBB(1) + Time>4h(1) + Weight<67kg(1)`

**Score Range:** 0–14

**Interpretation:**

- **0:** 30-day mortality ~0.8%
- **1–3:** Low risk (~2–7%)
- **4–6:** Intermediate risk (~12–16%)
- **7–8:** High risk (~23–30%)
- **≥9:** Very high risk (~35–50%+)

**Reference:** Morrow DA, Antman EM, Charlesworth A, et al. TIMI risk score for ST-elevation myocardial infarction: A convenient, bedside, clinical score for risk assessment at presentation. Circulation. 2000;102(17):2031-2037. PMID: 11044416

**Limitations:** Derived from fibrinolytic-era trial. May underestimate risk in primary PCI era. Some variables (weight) may be difficult to obtain rapidly. Does not include renal function or cardiac biomarkers beyond presentation.

