## Congestive Heart Failure, Hypertension, Age, Diabetes, Stroke–Vascular Disease, Age, Sex Category Score (CHA₂DS₂-VASc)

**Purpose:** Estimates annual stroke risk in patients with non-valvular atrial fibrillation to guide anticoagulation decisions.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Congestive heart failure (or LVEF ≤40%) | Clinical HF or reduced ejection fraction | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Hypertension | History of hypertension or BP >140/90 on treatment | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Age ≥75 years | Age 75 years or older | boolean | Yes/No | 2 |
| Diabetes mellitus | History of DM or fasting glucose >126 mg/dL or HbA1c ≥6.5% | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Stroke/TIA/thromboembolism | Prior history of ischemic stroke, TIA, or systemic thromboembolism | boolean | Yes/No | 2 |
| Vascular disease | Prior MI, PAD, or aortic plaque | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Age 65–74 years | Age between 65 and 74 years | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Sex category (female) | Female sex | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |

**Formula:** `CHA₂DS₂-VASc = CHF(1) + Hypertension(1) + Age_≥75(2) + Diabetes(1) + Stroke/TIA/VTE(2) + Vascular_disease(1) + Age_65-74(1) + Female_sex(1)`

**Score Range:** 0–9

**Interpretation:**

- **0 (male) or 1 (female only due to sex):** Low risk. Anticoagulation generally not recommended. Annual stroke risk ~0% (male) / ~0.6% (female).
- **1 (male) or 2 (female with 1 additional point):** Low-moderate risk. Consider anticoagulation based on individual factors. Annual stroke risk ~1.3%.
- **≥2 (male) or ≥3 (female):** Moderate-high risk. Oral anticoagulation recommended (DOAC preferred over warfarin). Annual stroke risk escalates: 2.2% (score 2), 3.2% (3), 4.0% (4), 6.7% (5), 9.8% (6), 9.6% (7), 12.5% (8), 15.2% (9).

**Reference:** Lip GYH, Nieuwlaat R, Pisters R, et al. Refining clinical risk stratification for predicting stroke and thromboembolism in atrial fibrillation using a novel risk factor-based approach: the Euro Heart Survey on Atrial Fibrillation. Chest. 2010;137(2):263-272. PMID: 19762550

**Limitations:** Low c-statistic (~0.6) for predicting stroke — discriminative ability is modest. Score of 1 in males vs. 1 solely from female sex have very different risk profiles. Does not account for AF burden (paroxysmal vs persistent). Most beneficial for identifying truly low-risk patients who can safely avoid anticoagulation.

