## Congestive Heart Failure, Hypertension, Age ≥75, Diabetes, Stroke Score (CHADS₂)

**Purpose:** Predecessor to CHA₂DS₂-VASc; estimates stroke risk in atrial fibrillation patients to guide anticoagulation.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Congestive heart failure | Clinical CHF or LVEF ≤40% | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Hypertension | History of hypertension | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Age ≥75 years | Age 75 or older | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Diabetes mellitus | History of DM | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Stroke/TIA history | Prior stroke or TIA | boolean | Yes/No | 2 |

**Formula:** `CHADS₂ = CHF(1) + Hypertension(1) + Age_≥75(1) + Diabetes(1) + Stroke/TIA(2)`

**Score Range:** 0–6

**Interpretation:**

- **0:** Low risk. Annual stroke rate ~1.9%. Consider aspirin or no therapy.
- **1:** Low-intermediate risk. Annual stroke rate ~2.8%. Consider anticoagulation.
- **≥2:** Moderate-high risk. Annual stroke rate 4.0–18.2%. Anticoagulation recommended.

**Reference:** Gage BF, Waterman AD, Shannon W, et al. Validation of clinical classification schemes for predicting stroke: results from the National Registry of Atrial Fibrillation. JAMA. 2001;285(22):2864-2870. PMID: 11401607

**Limitations:** Largely superseded by CHA₂DS₂-VASc. Score of 0 has limited discriminative ability — CHA₂DS₂-VASc better identifies truly low-risk patients. Does not include vascular disease, age 65–74, or sex. C-statistic ~0.6–0.7.

