## Outcomes Registry for Better Informed Treatment of Atrial Fibrillation Bleeding Score (ORBIT)

**Purpose:** Estimates major bleeding risk in AF patients, validated across both warfarin and DOAC-treated populations.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Age ≥75 | Age 75 or older | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Reduced hemoglobin/hematocrit | Hgb <13 g/dL (male) or <12 g/dL (female) or Hct <36% (male) or <36% (female) | boolean | Yes/No | 2 |
| eGFR <60 mL/min | Estimated GFR <60 mL/min/1.73m² | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Treatment with antiplatelet | Concurrent antiplatelet therapy | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Prior major bleed | History of major bleeding event | boolean | Yes/No | 2 |

**Formula:** `ORBIT = Age_≥75(1) + Reduced_Hgb(2) + eGFR<60(1) + Antiplatelet(1) + Prior_bleed(2)`

**Score Range:** 0–7

**Interpretation:**

- **0–2:** Low bleeding risk (~1–2.5% per year)
- **3:** Moderate risk (~4% per year)
- **4–7:** High risk (~6–8%+ per year)

**Reference:** O'Brien EC, Simon DN, Thomas LE, et al. The ORBIT bleeding score to stratify major bleeding risk in outpatients with atrial fibrillation: the ORBIT-AF registry. Am J Med. 2015;128(9):996.e9-996.e15. PMID: 25840038

**Limitations:** Developed in a US registry. Less commonly used than HAS-BLED. Not yet widely incorporated into guidelines. Does not include liver disease or alcohol.

