## CHA₂DS₂-VASc for use with Warfarin Time-in-Therapeutic Range (SAMe-TT₂R₂)

**Purpose:** Predicts which patients with AF on warfarin will have poor anticoagulation control (time in therapeutic range <65%), helping decide between warfarin and DOAC.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Sex (female) | Female sex | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Age (<60) | Age less than 60 years | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Medical history (>2 comorbidities) | More than 2 comorbidities (hypertension, DM, CAD, PAD, CHF, stroke, hepatic/renal disease, etc.) | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Treatment (interacting medications) | Use of interacting drugs (amiodarone, anticonvulsants, rifampin, etc.) | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Tobacco use (within 2 years) | Current or recent tobacco use | boolean | Yes/No | 2 |
| Racial/ethnic group (non-White) | Non-Caucasian race | boolean | Yes/No | 2 |

**Formula:** `SAMe-TT₂R₂ = Sex_female(1) + Age<60(1) + Medical_history>2(1) + Treatment_interacting(1) + Tobacco(2) + Race_nonWhite(2)`

**Score Range:** 0–8

**Interpretation:**

- **0–2:** Good TTR likely; warfarin is a reasonable option.
- **≥3:** Poor TTR predicted; consider DOAC instead of warfarin.

**Reference:** Lip GYH, Hagerty T, Haynes B, et al. Thromb Haemost. 2015;114(6):1242-1248. PMID: 26354844 (concept from Apostolakis S, et al. J Thromb Haemost. 2013;11:365-372)

**Limitations:** Race/ethnicity category is a crude variable with significant heterogeneity. Developed in warfarin-era; with increasing DOAC use, the tool's clinical utility may be decreasing. Score of 2 for non-White race may be seen as ethically problematic.

