## New York Heart Association Functional Classification (NYHA)

**Purpose:** Functional classification of heart failure based on symptom severity and exercise tolerance.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Functional capacity | Patient's subjective and objective exercise tolerance and symptoms | categorical | Class I–IV | single categorical grade I–IV |

**Formula:** `Categorical classification:
I = No limitation; ordinary physical activity does not cause symptoms
II = Slight limitation; comfortable at rest; ordinary activity causes symptoms
III = Marked limitation; comfortable at rest; less-than-ordinary activity causes symptoms
IV = Unable to carry out any physical activity without symptoms; symptoms at rest`

**Score Range:** I–IV

**Interpretation:**

- **I:** No limitation of physical activity
- **II:** Slight limitation; comfortable at rest
- **III:** Marked limitation; comfortable at rest
- **IV:** Symptoms at rest; any physical activity causes discomfort

**Reference:** Nomenclature and Criteria for Diagnosis of Diseases of the Heart and Great Vessels. New York Heart Association, 9th ed. Little, Brown & Co; 1994. (No single PMID — book publication)

**Limitations:** Subjective; significant inter-observer variability. Does not correlate perfectly with objective measures (e.g., peak VO₂, BNP). Patient classification can fluctuate day-to-day.

