## Meta-Analysis Global Group in Chronic Heart Failure Score (MAGGIC)

**Purpose:** Predicts 1-year and 3-year mortality in patients with chronic heart failure using individual patient data from 39,372 patients.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Age | Age in years | years | continuous | non-linear point assignment increasing with age |
| Sex | Male or female | boolean | Male/Female | Male = higher risk |
| LVEF | Left ventricular ejection fraction | % | continuous; cutoffs at 19.5%, 24.5%, 29.5%, 34.5%, 39.5% | non-linear (lower EF = more points) |
| NYHA class | NYHA functional class I–IV | categorical | I, II, III, IV | I = fewest points; IV = most points |
| Diuretic use | Whether on diuretics | boolean | Yes/No | adds points if yes |
| Systolic BP | Systolic blood pressure (mmHg) | mmHg | continuous | non-linear (lower SBP = more points) |
| BMI | Body mass index | kg/m² | continuous | non-linear (higher BMI = fewer points — obesity paradox) |
| Serum creatinine | Creatinine level | mg/dL | continuous | non-linear (higher Cr = more points) |
| Time since HF diagnosis | Duration of HF in months | months | continuous | non-linear |
| Smoking status | Current smoker | boolean | Yes/No | adds points |
| COPD | History of COPD | boolean | Yes/No | adds points |
| Diabetes | History of diabetes | boolean | Yes/No | adds points |

**Formula:** `Complex lookup table with non-linear point assignments for each variable; total points mapped to 1-year and 3-year mortality probabilities. No simple closed-form equation; use published nomogram or online calculator. The score sums the individual variable point assignments.`

**Score Range:** 0–50+ (higher = higher risk)

**Interpretation:**

- **Low total:** 1-year mortality ~5–10%
- **Intermediate total:** 1-year mortality ~15–30%
- **High total:** 1-year mortality ~40–70%

**Reference:** Pocock SJ, Ariti CA, McMurray JJV, et al. Predicting survival in heart failure: a risk score based on 39,372 patients from 30 studies. Eur Heart J. 2013;34(19):1404-1413. PMID: 23300255

**Limitations:** Complex (requires lookup table or calculator). Derived primarily from clinical trial populations (may not represent real-world HF patients). Some variables (e.g., time since HF diagnosis) may be difficult to ascertain. Originally validated in HFrEF; HFpEF validation less robust.

