## Seattle Heart Failure Model (SHFM)

**Purpose:** Quantitative model predicting 1-, 2-, and 3-year survival in heart failure patients, incorporating medications, devices, and laboratory values.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Age | Age in years | years | continuous | coefficient −0.0247 per year |
| Sex | Male = 1 point | boolean | Male/Female | Male = +0.3003 |
| NYHA class | NYHA class III vs IV (reference I/II) | categorical | I/II, III, IV | III = +0.2068; IV = +0.6983 |
| LVEF | Left ventricular ejection fraction (%) | % | 0–100 | −0.0215 per 1% increase |
| Systolic BP | Systolic blood pressure (mmHg) | mmHg | continuous | −0.0115 per mmHg increase |
| Diuretic dose (furosemide equivalent) | Daily furosemide dose or equivalent | mg/day | 0–500+ mg | +0.0018 per mg |
| Serum sodium | Serum sodium (mEq/L) | mEq/L | 120–150 | −0.0528 per mEq/L increase |
| Serum creatinine | Serum creatinine (mg/dL) | mg/dL | 0.5–5+ | +0.1857 per mg/dL |
| Total cholesterol | Total cholesterol (mg/dL) | mg/dL | 100–400+ | −0.0036 per mg/dL |
| Hemoglobin | Hemoglobin (g/dL) | g/dL | 6–18 | −0.0701 per g/dL |
| Lymphocyte percentage | Percentage of lymphocytes on WBC differential | % | 1–60 | −0.0185 per % |
| Uric acid | Serum uric acid (mg/dL) | mg/dL | 3–15+ | verify exact coefficient |
| ACE-inhibitor/ARB use | Current use | boolean | Yes/No | −0.1856 if yes |
| Beta-blocker use | Current use | boolean | Yes/No | −0.2860 if yes |
| Allopurinol use | Current use | boolean | Yes/No | +0.1875 if yes |
| Statins | Current use | boolean | Yes/No | −0.1980 if yes |

**Formula:** `Linear predictor (LP) = Σ(coefficients × variable values). Then: 1-year survival = S₀(1)^exp(LP − mean_LP). S₀(1) = baseline 1-year survival at mean LP. Exact S₀ values and all coefficients are published in the original paper and calculator. Verify precise coefficients and baseline survival functions from Levy WC, et al. 2006.`

**Score Range:** Continuous survival probability (0–100%)

**Interpretation:**

- **1-year survival >90%:** Low annual mortality risk
- **1-year survival 70–90%:** Moderate risk
- **1-year survival <50%:** High risk; consider advanced therapies (LVAD, transplant evaluation)

**Reference:** Levy WC, Mozaffarian D, Linker DT, et al. The Seattle Heart Failure Model: prediction of survival in heart failure. Circulation. 2006;113(11):1424-1433. PMID: 16534094

**Limitations:** Requires multiple lab values and medication data. Original derivation from clinical trial populations. Less validated in HFpEF. Does not capture right ventricular function, iron status, or advanced biomarkers (galectin-3, ST2). Online calculator required for precise predictions.

