## Heart Failure Survival Score (HFSS)

**Purpose:** Risk stratifies chronic HF patients for 1-year survival to identify candidates for cardiac transplantation.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Cause of HF (ischemic) | Ischemic etiology | boolean | Yes/No | +0.6931 |
| Resting heart rate | Heart rate at rest (bpm) | bpm | continuous | +0.0216 per bpm |
| LVEF | Left ventricular ejection fraction (%) | % | 0–100 | −0.0464 per % |
| Mean BP | Mean arterial blood pressure (mmHg) | mmHg | continuous | −0.0255 per mmHg |
| Peak VO₂ | Peak oxygen consumption on cardiopulmonary exercise testing (mL/kg/min) | mL/kg/min | 5–30+ | −0.0546 per mL/kg/min |
| Serum sodium | Serum sodium (mEq/L) | mEq/L | 120–150 | −0.0470 per mEq/L |
| QRS duration | QRS duration on ECG (ms) | ms | 60–200+ | +0.0074 per ms |

**Formula:** `HFSS = Ischemic_cause(0.6931) + HR(0.0216 × bpm) + LVEF(−0.0464 × %) + MAP(−0.0255 × mmHg) + Peak_VO2(−0.0546 × mL/kg/min) + Sodium(−0.0470 × mEq/L) + QRS(0.0074 × ms). Then: Risk score = exp(HFSS); 1-year survival = S₀^risk_score where S₀ is the baseline survival constant.`

**Score Range:** Continuous; risk score typically 0–15+

**Interpretation:**

- **<8.10:** Low risk: 1-year survival >90% (transplant can be deferred)
- **8.10–11.4:** Medium risk: 1-year survival 70–90% (consider transplant listing)
- **>11.4:** High risk: 1-year survival <70% (urgent transplant evaluation)

**Reference:** Aaronson KD, Schwartz JS, Chen TM, et al. Development and prospective validation of a clinical index to predict survival in ambulatory patients referred for cardiac transplant evaluation. Circulation. 1997;95(12):2660-2667. PMID: 9193435

**Limitations:** Requires cardiopulmonary exercise testing (peak VO₂) — not available in all settings. Derived from single-center transplant referral population. Not validated in HFpEF. BNP/NT-proBNP not included.

