## H2FPEF Score

**Purpose:** Diagnoses heart failure with preserved ejection fraction (HFpEF) in patients with unexplained dyspnea and LVEF ≥50%.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Heavy (BMI) | Body mass index | kg/m² | continuous; points assigned by BMI cutoffs | BMI 20.0–24.9 = 0; 25.0–29.9 = 1; 30.0–34.9 = 2; 35.0–39.9 = 3; ≥40 = 4 |
| Hypertensive | On ≥1 antihypertensive medication | boolean | Yes/No | 2 |
| AF (atrial fibrillation) | Paroxysmal or persistent/permanent AF | boolean | Yes/No | 3 |
| Pulmonary hypertension (PASP >35 mmHg) | Doppler estimated pulmonary artery systolic pressure >35 mmHg on echo | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Age >60 | Age greater than 60 years | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| E/e' ratio >9 | Echocardiographic ratio of mitral inflow E velocity to tissue Doppler e' velocity | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |

**Formula:** `H2FPEF = Heavy_BMI(0-4) + Hypertensive(2) + AF(3) + Pulmonary_HTN(1) + Age>60(1) + E/e'>9(1)`

**Score Range:** 0–9

**Interpretation:**

- **0–1:** Low probability of HFpEF (P(HFpEF) <25%). Consider alternative diagnoses.
- **2–5:** Intermediate probability (25–75%). Further invasive hemodynamic testing (RHC) recommended.
- **6–9:** High probability of HFpEF (>90%). Diagnosis likely confirmed.

**Reference:** Reddy YNV, Carter RE, Obokata M, et al. A simple, evidence-based approach to help guide diagnosis of heart failure with preserved ejection fraction. Circulation. 2018;138(9):861-870. PMID: 29792299

**Limitations:** Requires echocardiographic parameters (E/e', PASP). Developed at a single center (Mayo Clinic) with highly selected patients. Intermediate scores (2–5) still require invasive testing. Not yet validated in acute HF or post-discharge settings.

