## Pooled Cohort Equations for ASCVD Risk (PCE / ASCVD Risk Calculator)

**Purpose:** Estimates 10-year risk of a first atherosclerotic cardiovascular event (MI or stroke) in primary prevention patients aged 40–79.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Age | Age in years | years | 40–79 | ln(age) × sex/race-specific coefficient |
| Sex | Male or female | categorical | Male/Female | sex-specific coefficients and baseline survival |
| Race | White or African American | categorical | White/Black | race-specific coefficients |
| Total cholesterol | Total cholesterol (mg/dL) | mg/dL | 100–400+ | ln(TC) × sex/race-specific coefficient |
| HDL-C | HDL cholesterol (mg/dL) | mg/dL | 20–100+ | ln(HDL) × sex/race-specific coefficient |
| Systolic BP | Systolic blood pressure (mmHg) | mmHg | 90–200+ | ln(SBP) × coefficient, with separate term for BP treatment status |
| BP treatment | Whether on antihypertensive medication | boolean | Yes/No | treatment × ln(SBP) interaction coefficient |
| Diabetes | History of diabetes mellitus | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient (0 or 1) |
| Current smoker | Current cigarette smoking | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient (0 or 1) + age × smoking interaction term |

**Formula:** `10-year ASCVD risk = 1 − S₀(10)^exp(individual_sum − mean_sum)

Where:
- individual_sum = β₁×ln(age) + β₂×ln(TC) + β₃×ln(HDL) + β₄×ln(SBP)×(on_treatment) + β₅×ln(SBP)×(not_treatment) + β₆×diabetes + β₇×smoker + β₈×ln(age)×ln(TC) + β₉×ln(age)×ln(HDL) + β₁₀×ln(age)×ln(SBP)×(on_treatment) + β₁₁×ln(age)×ln(SBP)×(not_treatment) + β₁₂×ln(age)×smoker
- Race- and sex-specific β coefficients and S₀(10) baselines are published in Goff et al. 2013, Supplementary Appendix.
- For White males: S₀(10) = 0.91436
- For White females: S₀(10) = 0.96652
- For Black males: S₀(10) = 0.89536
- For Black females: S₀(10) = 0.95334
- Coefficients: verify all exact β values from the published supplementary tables (too numerous to list fully here — 12 coefficients × 4 race-sex groups = 48 values).`

**Score Range:** 0–100% (10-year risk)

**Interpretation:**

- **<5%:** Low 10-year ASCVD risk
- **5–7.4%:** Borderline risk
- **7.5–19.9%:** Intermediate risk — statin therapy recommended per ACC/AHA guidelines
- **≥20%:** High risk — statin therapy and aggressive risk factor modification recommended

**Reference:** Goff DC Jr, Lloyd-Jones DM, Bennett G, et al. 2013 ACC/AHA guideline on the assessment of cardiovascular risk. Circulation. 2014;129(25 Suppl 2):S49-S73. PMID: 24222018

**Limitations:** Tends to overestimate risk in some contemporary cohorts. Not validated for race/ethnicities other than White and African American (e.g., Hispanic, Asian). Not applicable to patients with established CVD (secondary prevention). Age limited to 40–79. Does not incorporate family history, CRP, CAC score, or social determinants of health. Performance varies by subgroup.

