## Framingham Risk Score (2008 General Cardiovascular Risk Profile) (FRS)

**Purpose:** Estimates 10-year risk of a first cardiovascular event (coronary death, MI, stroke, heart failure, or peripheral vascular disease).

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Age | Age in years | years | 30–74 | sex-specific points assigned by age decade |
| Total cholesterol | Total cholesterol (mg/dL) | mg/dL | continuous | sex-specific points |
| HDL-C | HDL cholesterol (mg/dL) | mg/dL | continuous | sex-specific points |
| Systolic BP | Systolic blood pressure (mmHg), stratified by treatment status | mmHg | continuous | sex-specific points, separate for treated/untreated |
| Smoking status | Current smoker | boolean | Yes/No | sex-specific points |
| Diabetes | History of DM | boolean | Yes/No | sex-specific points |

**Formula:** `Point-based system: assign points for each risk factor per sex-specific lookup tables, then sum. Map total points to 10-year CVD risk from published tables. Cox model underlying: h(t) = h₀(t) × exp(β₁X₁ + β₂X₂ + ...). Exact coefficients published in D'Agostino RB, et al. 2008. Total points → 10-year risk % from published conversion table.`

**Score Range:** −3 to +20+ points (sex-specific)

**Interpretation:**

- **<10 points (male) / <13 (female):** Low risk (<10% 10-year CVD risk)
- **10–14 (male) / 13–19 (female):** Intermediate risk (10–20%)
- **≥15 (male) / ≥20 (female):** High risk (>20% 10-year CVD risk)

**Reference:** D'Agostino RB Sr, Vasan RS, Pencina MJ, et al. General cardiovascular risk profile for use in primary care: the Framingham Heart Study. Circulation. 2008;117(6):743-753. PMID: 18212285

**Limitations:** Developed primarily in a White, middle-class New England cohort. May overestimate or underestimate risk in other populations. Does not include family history, social determinants, or biomarkers. Multiple versions exist (CHD-specific vs general CVD) — use the 2008 general profile. Not validated in patients <30 or >74 years.

