## SCORE2 (Systematic COronary Risk Evaluation 2)

**Purpose:** Estimates 10-year risk of first fatal and non-fatal cardiovascular events (MI, stroke) in apparently healthy adults aged 40–69 in Europe.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Age | Age in years | years | 40–69 | calibration factor by age and region |
| Sex | Male or female | categorical | Male/Female | sex-specific model |
| Smoking status | Current smoker | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient |
| Systolic BP | Systolic blood pressure (mmHg) | mmHg | continuous | coefficient |
| Non-HDL cholesterol | Non-HDL cholesterol (mmol/L) = Total cholesterol − HDL-C | mmol/L | continuous | coefficient |

**Formula:** `10-year risk = 1 − S₀(10)^exp(individual_linear_predictor). Coefficients are published in SCORE2 manuscript and risk chart lookup tables. Calibration factors applied based on WHO cardiovascular mortality risk region (low, moderate, high, very high). Use published risk charts or ESC CVD Risk Calculation app for precise values.`

**Score Range:** 0–100% (10-year risk)

**Interpretation:**

- **<2.5% (age <50) / <5% (age 50–69) for low-risk countries:** Low risk
- **2.5–7.4% (age <50) / 5–9.9% (age 50–69):** Moderate risk
- **≥7.5% (age <50) / ≥10% (age 50–69):** High risk — consider statin therapy
- **≥10% (age <50) / ≥15% (age 50–69):** Very high risk

**Reference:** SCORE2 working group and ESC Cardiovascular Risk Collaboration. SCORE2 risk prediction algorithms: new models to estimate 10-year risk of cardiovascular disease in Europe. Eur Heart J. 2021;42(25):2439-2454. PMID: 33871026

**Limitations:** Designed for European populations; not directly applicable to US, Asian, or other populations. Age limited to 40–69 (use SCORE2-OP for ≥70). Does not include diabetes (separate SCORE2-Diabetes model published separately). Non-HDL-C may not be routinely reported in all labs.

