## PROCAM Risk Score (Prospective Cardiovascular Münster Study)

**Purpose:** Estimates 10-year risk of major coronary events (MI or cardiac death) using a German occupational cohort.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Age | Age in years | years | continuous | coefficient in logistic model |
| LDL-C | LDL cholesterol (mg/dL) | mg/dL | continuous | coefficient |
| Smoking | Current smoker | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient |
| HDL-C | HDL cholesterol (mg/dL) | mg/dL | continuous | inverse coefficient |
| Systolic BP | Systolic blood pressure (mmHg) | mmHg | continuous | coefficient |
| Family history of premature MI | MI in first-degree relative (male <60, female <65) | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient |
| Diabetes mellitus | History of DM | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient |
| Triglycerides | Triglycerides (mg/dL) | mg/dL | continuous | coefficient |

**Formula:** `Logistic regression: Risk = 1/(1 + exp(−(β₀ + β₁×age + β₂×LDL + β₃×smoking + β₄×HDL + β₅×SBP + β₆×FH + β₇×DM + β₈×TG))). Exact coefficients published in Assmann G, et al. 2002. Point-based simplified version also published.`

**Score Range:** 0–100% (10-year risk); point system 0–50+

**Interpretation:**

- **<10% (10-year risk):** Low risk
- **10–20%:** Intermediate risk
- **>20%:** High risk — treat aggressively

**Reference:** Assmann G, Cullen P, Schulte H. Simple scoring scheme for calculating the risk of acute coronary events based on the 10-year follow-up of the prospective cardiovascular Münster (PROCAM) study. Circulation. 2002;105(3):310-315. PMID: 11804985

**Limitations:** Originally derived from male workers only — later adapted for women. German occupational cohort may not generalize to all populations. Includes triglycerides (not in most other calculators). Family history definition varies by study.

