## European System for Cardiac Operative Risk Evaluation II (EuroSCORE II)

**Purpose:** Predicts in-hospital mortality after cardiac surgery (CABG, valve, or combined procedures).

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Age | Age in years | years | continuous | logistic coefficient (non-linear by decade) |
| Sex (female) | Female sex | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient |
| Insulin-dependent diabetes | DM on insulin therapy | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient |
| NYHA class | NYHA class I–IV | categorical | I–IV | increasing coefficients |
| CCS class 4 angina | Canadian Cardiovascular Society angina class 4 | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient |
| Critical preoperative state | Ventricular tachycardia, cardiac massage, ventilation, inotropes, IABP, acute renal failure | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient |
| Extracardiac arteriopathy | PAD, carotid disease, or aortic aneurysm | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient |
| Poor mobility | Severe impairment of mobility due to musculoskeletal or neurological dysfunction | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient |
| Previous cardiac surgery | Prior cardiac surgery (redo sternotomy) | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient |
| Chronic pulmonary disease | Long-term bronchodilator or steroid use for lung disease | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient |
| Active endocarditis | Still on antibiotics for endocarditis at time of surgery | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient |
| Priority | Surgical urgency | categorical | elective / urgent / emergency / salvage | increasing coefficients |
| LV function (LVEF) | Left ventricular ejection fraction | categorical | Good(>50%) / Moderate(31–50%) / Poor(21–30%) / Very poor(≤20%) | increasing coefficients |
| Recent MI (<90 days) | Myocardial infarction within 90 days of surgery | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient |
| Pulmonary artery systolic pressure | PASP in mmHg | categorical | ≤30 / 31–55 / ≥55 mmHg | increasing coefficients |
| Procedure type | Type of cardiac surgical procedure | categorical | isolated CABG / isolated non-CABG / 2 procedures / 3+ procedures | increasing coefficients |
| Renal dysfunction (Cr or dialysis) | Creatinine clearance category or on dialysis | categorical | CrCl>85 / 51–85 / ≤50 / dialysis | increasing coefficients |
| Neurological dysfunction | Disease severely affecting ambulation or upper extremity function | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient |

**Formula:** `Logistic model: Predicted mortality = e^(β₀ + Σβᵢxᵢ) / (1 + e^(β₀ + Σβᵢxᵢ)). β₀ = −5.324537. All individual β coefficients for 18 variables are published in Nashef SAM, et al. 2012, supplementary tables. Use the online EuroSCORE II calculator for precise computation (euroscore.org).`

**Score Range:** 0–100% predicted mortality

**Interpretation:**

- **<2%:** Low operative risk
- **2–5%:** Moderate risk
- **5–10%:** High risk
- **>10%:** Very high risk

**Reference:** Nashef SAM, Roques F, Sharples LD, et al. EuroSCORE II. Eur J Cardiothorac Surg. 2012;41(4):734-744. PMID: 22378855

**Limitations:** Multiple variables require nuanced clinical judgment (e.g., 'poor mobility'). May overestimate risk in some contemporary cohorts with improved outcomes. Does not capture frailty, porcelain aorta, or liver disease. Designed for in-hospital mortality, not long-term outcomes. Less validated for TAVR or minimally invasive procedures.

