## Society of Thoracic Surgeons Risk Score (STS Score)

**Purpose:** Predicts operative mortality and morbidity after cardiac surgery (CABG, valve, combined) using the STS national database.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Demographics | Age, sex, race, height, weight, BMI | mixed | continuous | multivariable coefficients in logistic model |
| Risk factors and comorbidities | DM, hypertension, dyslipidemia, renal failure/dialysis, cerebrovascular disease, peripheral vascular disease, chronic lung disease, immunosuppression, endocarditis, etc. | mixed | multiple binary and continuous variables | multivariable coefficients |
| Cardiac-specific variables | NYHA class, CCS class, LVEF, prior MI, arrhythmias, number of diseased vessels, left main disease, cardiogenic shock, IABP/vent support, etc. | mixed | multiple variables | multivariable coefficients |
| Procedural variables | Urgency, procedure type, reoperation, etc. | mixed | multiple variables | multivariable coefficients |

**Formula:** `Complex multivariable logistic regression model with 40+ variables. Predicted risk = 1/(1 + exp(−(β₀ + Σβᵢxᵢ))). Separate models for isolated CABG, isolated valve, CABG+valve, and other procedures. Coefficients updated periodically from the STS national database. Calculator available at riskcalc.sts.org/stswebriskcalc/`

**Score Range:** 0–100% predicted operative mortality and morbidity

**Interpretation:**

- **<1%:** Low operative mortality risk
- **1–5%:** Moderate risk
- **5–10%:** High risk
- **>10%:** Very high risk

**Reference:** Shahian DM, O'Brien SM, Filardo G, et al. The Society of Thoracic Surgeons 2008 cardiac surgery risk models: part 1 — coronary artery bypass grafting surgery. Ann Thorac Surg. 2009;88(1 Suppl):S23-S62. PMID: 19559822

**Limitations:** US-specific (derived from US hospitals); may not perform well internationally. Extremely complex — requires dedicated calculator. Updated periodically (older versions may underestimate contemporary outcomes). Does not capture all frailty measures. Not designed for TAVR or off-pump CABG (separate models exist).

