## SYNTAX Score

**Purpose:** Quantifies coronary artery disease complexity to guide revascularization strategy (PCI vs CABG) in patients with left main and/or three-vessel disease.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Coronary lesion characteristics | Each coronary lesion scored for: dominance, lesion location, number of lesions, total occlusion, trifurcation, bifurcation, aorto-ostial, severe tortuosity, length >20mm, heavy calcification, thrombus, diffuse disease | categorical | Multiple scored items per lesion based on the 12-item SYNTAX algorithm | Points assigned per lesion characteristic (detailed in SYNTAX score working group) |

**Formula:** `Sum of all lesion-specific points from the coronary anatomy (12-item algorithm applied to each lesion, then summed). Full algorithm published by SYNTAX working group and available at syntaxscore.com. Each lesion adds 0–20+ points depending on characteristics. Total is sum across all lesions in the coronary tree.`

**Score Range:** 0–80+ (approximately)

**Interpretation:**

- **0–22:** Low complexity. PCI and CABG have similar outcomes. PCI is reasonable.
- **23–32:** Intermediate complexity. CABG preferred in most patients.
- **≥33:** High complexity. CABG strongly recommended over PCI.

**Reference:** Sianos G, Morel MA, Kappetein AP, et al. The SYNTAX Score: an angiographic tool grading the complexity of coronary artery disease. EuroIntervention. 2005;1(2):219-227. PMID: 19758907 (score algorithm); SYNTAX Trial: Serruys PW, et al. N Engl J Med. 2009;360:961-972. PMID: 19228615

**Limitations:** Requires angiographic interpretation by experienced interventional cardiologist (significant inter-observer variability). Does not include clinical variables (SYNTAX Score II adds clinical factors). Only applicable to left main and/or 3-vessel disease. Does not account for ischemia (FFR).

---

## SYNTAX Score II (SYNTAX II)

**Purpose:** Integrates anatomic SYNTAX score with clinical variables to predict 4-year mortality after PCI or CABG, guiding individualized revascularization.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| SYNTAX Score (anatomic) | Original anatomic SYNTAX score from coronary angiogram | points | 0–80+ | coefficient in model |
| Age | Age in years | years | continuous | coefficient |
| Sex (female) | Female sex | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient |
| CrCl (Cockcroft-Gault) | Creatinine clearance | mL/min | continuous | coefficient |
| LVEF | Left ventricular ejection fraction | % | continuous | coefficient |
| COPD | Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient |
| Peripheral vascular disease | PAD | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient |

**Formula:** `Nomogram-based: predicted 4-year mortality is derived from the combination of SYNTAX Score and 6 clinical variables via a Cox regression model. Coefficients published in Farooq V, et al. 2013. Use the online calculator at syntaxscore.com for precise predictions. PCI recommendation: if SYNTAX II 4-year mortality is lower with PCI than CABG → PCI; otherwise → CABG.`

**Score Range:** 0–100% predicted 4-year mortality

**Interpretation:**

- **PCI predicted mortality < CABG predicted mortality:** Recommend PCI
- **CABG predicted mortality ≤ PCI predicted mortality:** Recommend CABG

**Reference:** Farooq V, van Klaveren D, Steyerberg EW, et al. Anatomical and clinical characteristics to guide decision making between coronary artery bypass surgery and percutaneous coronary intervention for individual patients: development and validation of SYNTAX score II. Lancet. 2013;381(9867):639-650. PMID: 23439009

**Limitations:** Requires both angiographic scoring and clinical data. Validated primarily in left main/3-vVD. Decision-making between PCI and CABG should incorporate Heart Team discussion, not rely solely on SYNTAX II. Inter-observer variability in SYNTAX score applies.

