## Revised Cardiac Risk Index (RCRI / Lee Index)

**Purpose:** Estimates risk of major cardiac complications (MI, cardiac arrest, pulmonary edema, complete heart block, ventricular fibrillation) after non-cardiac surgery.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| High-risk surgery | Intraperitoneal, intrathoracic, or suprainguinal vascular surgery | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Ischemic heart disease | History of MI, positive stress test, current chest pain due to myocardial ischemia, use of nitroglycerin, ECG with pathological Q waves, or prior PCI/CABG | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Congestive heart failure | History of CHF, pulmonary edema, paroxysmal nocturnal dyspnea, S3 gallop, bilateral rales, or CXR showing pulmonary vascular redistribution | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Cerebrovascular disease | History of TIA or stroke | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Preoperative insulin therapy | Insulin-treated diabetes mellitus | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Preoperative serum creatinine >2.0 mg/dL | Renal dysfunction (Cr >2.0 mg/dL or >177 µmol/L) | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |

**Formula:** `RCRI = High_risk_surgery(1) + Ischemic_HD(1) + CHF(1) + CVD(1) + Insulin_DM(1) + Cr>2.0(1)`

**Score Range:** 0–6

**Interpretation:**

- **0:** Very low risk (~3.9% major cardiac complications)
- **1:** Low risk (~6.0%)
- **2:** Moderate risk (~10.1%)
- **≥3:** High risk (~15–30%+)

**Reference:** Lee TH, Marcantonio ER, Mangione CM, et al. Derivation and prospective validation of a simple index for prediction of cardiac risk of major noncardiac surgery. Circulation. 1999;100(10):1043-1049. PMID: 10477528

**Limitations:** Moderate discriminative ability (c-statistic ~0.6–0.7). Does not include functional capacity, type of surgery within categories, or biomarkers. Original derivation from 1990s. Newer scores (NSQIP, VSG-CRI) may perform better. Does not predict 30-day mortality — only in-hospital cardiac complications.

