## American College of Surgeons National Surgical Quality Improvement Program Surgical Risk Calculator (ACS NSQIP)

**Purpose:** Predicts 8 postoperative outcomes (including serious complications, cardiac complications, pneumonia, death) for specific CPT-coded surgical procedures.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| CPT code | Current Procedural Terminology code for the specific surgery | categorical | Specific CPT codes from the NSQIP database | procedure-specific baseline risk |
| Age | Patient age | years | continuous | coefficient |
| Sex | Male/Female | categorical | Male/Female | coefficient |
| Functional status | Functional status before surgery | categorical | Independent / Partially dependent / Totally dependent | coefficient |
| ASA class | ASA physical status classification | categorical | 1–5 | coefficient |
| Steroid use | Chronic steroid use for immunosuppression | boolean | Yes/No | coefficient |
| Sepsis | Sepsis within 48 hours preoperatively | categorical | None / SIRS / Sepsis / Septic shock | coefficient |
| Additional comorbidities | 12 additional variables: ascites, ventilator dependence, disseminated cancer, diabetes, hypertension, COPD, CHF, dyspnea, smoke, dialysis, acute renal failure, BMI, etc. | mixed | various | multivariable coefficients |

**Formula:** `Multivariable logistic regression: predicted risk = 1/(1 + exp(−(β₀ + Σβᵢxᵢ))). Separate models for each of 8 outcomes. Over 1.4 million cases from 680+ hospitals used to derive coefficients. Use calculator at riskcalculator.facs.org/`

**Score Range:** 0–100% risk for each of 8 outcomes

**Interpretation:**

- **Varies by outcome and procedure:** Provides individualized risk estimates for: serious complication, any complication, pneumonia, cardiac complication, surgical site infection, UTI, VTE, renal failure, readmission, death

**Reference:** Bilimoria KY, Liu Y, Paruch JL, et al. Development and evaluation of the universal ACS NSQIP surgical risk calculator: a decision aid and informed consent source for patients and surgeons. J Am Coll Surg. 2013;217(5):833-842. PMID: 24055393

**Limitations:** Requires CPT code (procedure-specific). May overestimate or underestimate risk for rare procedures. Does not capture all surgeon-specific or hospital-specific factors. Updated periodically. Used for informed consent and shared decision-making, not as a sole decision tool.

