## Mehran Risk Score for Contrast-Induced Nephropathy (Mehran Score)

**Purpose:** Predicts risk of contrast-induced nephropathy (CIN) after percutaneous coronary intervention.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Hypotension | SBP <80 mmHg requiring inotropes or IABP for ≥1 hour (within 24h post-procedure) | boolean | Yes/No | 5 |
| Intra-aortic balloon pump use | IABP use | boolean | Yes/No | 5 |
| CHF (Class III/IV or history of pulmonary edema) | Congestive heart failure | boolean | Yes/No | 5 |
| Age >75 years | Age over 75 | boolean | Yes/No | 4 |
| Anemia | Hematocrit <39% (male) or <36% (female) | boolean | Yes/No | 3 |
| Diabetes mellitus | History of DM | boolean | Yes/No | 3 |
| Contrast volume | Volume of contrast media (mL) | mL | continuous | 1 point per 100 mL |
| Serum creatinine >1.5 mg/dL | Baseline creatinine >1.5 mg/dL | boolean | Yes/No | 4 |
| eGFR <60 mL/min | Estimated GFR <60 | boolean | Yes/No | additional risk modifier |

**Formula:** `Mehran = Hypotension(5) + IABP(5) + CHF(5) + Age>75(4) + Anemia(3) + DM(3) + Contrast_volume(1 per 100mL) + Cr>1.5(4)`

**Score Range:** 0–30+

**Interpretation:**

- **≤5:** Low risk (~7.5% CIN risk)
- **6–10:** Moderate risk (~14%)
- **11–15:** High risk (~26%)
- **≥16:** Very high risk (~57% CIN risk; ~13% dialysis needed)

**Reference:** Mehran R, Aymong ED, Nikolsky E, et al. A simple risk score for prediction of contrast-induced nephropathy after percutaneous coronary intervention: development and initial validation. J Am Coll Cardiol. 2004;44(7):1393-1399. PMID: 15464318

**Limitations:** Derived from PCI population — less validated for contrast CT. Contrast volume estimation may be imprecise pre-procedure. Does not capture hydration strategy or type of contrast (iso-osmolar vs low-osmolar). Pre-dates routine use of pre-hydration protocols.

