## Parsonnet Score

**Purpose:** Preoperative risk stratification for mortality in cardiac surgery, originally developed for valvular surgery.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Age | Points assigned by age decades (highest for >70) | years | by decade | 0–14 points by age |
| Sex (female) | Female sex | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Diabetes (insulin-dependent) | Insulin-dependent DM | boolean | Yes/No | 3 |
| Hypertension | HTN >140/90 on treatment | boolean | Yes/No | 2 |
| LVEF | Ejection fraction | categorical | Good(>50) / Fair(30–49) / Poor(20–29) / Very poor(<20) | 0–12 by category |
| Preoperative IABP | IABP in place | boolean | Yes/No | 2 |
| Left main stenosis >70% | Left main CAD | boolean | Yes/No | 3 |
| Reoperation | Redo cardiac surgery | categorical | First / Second / Third+ | 5–10 |
| Preoperative use of inotropes | IV inotropes at time of surgery | boolean | Yes/No | 3 |
| Dialysis-dependent renal failure | On chronic dialysis | boolean | Yes/No | 2 |
| Body habitus (morbid obesity) | BMI >35 or >1.5× ideal body weight | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Valvular disease specifics | Mitral valve vs aortic valve pathology | categorical | various | varies |
| Emergency surgery | Emergent procedure | boolean | Yes/No | 3 |
| Other risk factors | COPD, pulmonary hypertension, etc. | mixed | various | various |

**Formula:** `Sum of individual risk factor points. Detailed point assignments published in Parsonnet V, et al. 1989. Not a simple additive formula — some items are interactions. Total score mapped to predicted mortality via published tables.`

**Score Range:** 0–100+ (mortality prediction ~1–50%+)

**Interpretation:**

- **<4:** Low operative risk (<2% mortality)
- **4–14:** Moderate risk (2–5%)
- **≥15:** High risk (>5% mortality)

**Reference:** Parsonnet V, Dean D, Bernstein AD. A method of uniform stratification of risk for evaluating the results of surgery in acquired adult heart disease. Circulation. 1989;79(6 Pt 2):I3-I12. PMID: 2720932

**Limitations:** Historical — largely superseded by EuroSCORE II and STS Score. Derivation from single center in 1980s (outdated operative mortality). Does not capture modern techniques. Some variables are subjective. Complex point assignments not all intuitive.

