## Logistic Organ Dysfunction System (LODS)

**Purpose:** Quantifies severity of organ dysfunction in ICU patients with a logistic model calibrated for hospital mortality prediction.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Neurological | GCS | score | GCS 3–4=5; 5–7=3; 8–10=2; 11–13=1; 14–15=0 | 0–5 |
| Cardiovascular | Heart rate, SBP, cardiac arrest | mixed | Various combinations scored 0–5 | 0–5 |
| Renal | Urea and urine output | mixed | Various | 0–5 |
| Pulmonary | PaO₂/FiO₂ and mechanical ventilation | mixed | Various | 0–5 |
| Hematologic | WBC and platelets | mixed | Various | 0–5 |
| Hepatic | Bilirubin and prothrombin time | mixed | Various | 0–5 |

**Formula:** `LODS = Sum of organ-specific scores (0–5 per organ, 6 organs). Logistic model: logit = −5.7865 + 0.1374 × LODS + diagnostic category coefficients. Predicted mortality = e^logit / (1 + e^logit).`

**Score Range:** 0–22

**Interpretation:**

- **0–5:** Low predicted hospital mortality
- **6–12:** Moderate mortality
- **>12:** High predicted mortality

**Reference:** Le Gall JR, Klar J, Lemeshow S, et al. The Logistic Organ Dysfunction system: a new way to assess organ dysfunction in the intensive care unit. JAMA. 1996;276(10):802-810. PMID: 8769590

**Limitations:** Complex scoring. Superseded by SAPS 3 and SOFA in clinical use. Original calibration from 1990s data.

---

## Multiple Organ Dysfunction Score (MODS)

**Purpose:** Describes and quantifies organ dysfunction over time in ICU patients, using six organ systems.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Respiratory | PaO₂/FiO₂ ratio | mmHg | >300=0; 226–300=1; 151–225=2; 76–150=3; ≤75=4 | 0–4 |
| Renal | Serum creatinine (mg/dL) | mg/dL | <1.1=0; 1.1–2.3=1; 2.3–4.0=2; 4.0–5.7=3; >5.7=4 | 0–4 |
| Hepatic | Serum bilirubin (mg/dL) | mg/dL | <1.1=0; 1.1–2.3=1; 2.3–4.0=2; 4.0–5.7=3; >5.7=4 | 0–4 |
| Cardiovascular | Pressure-adjusted heart rate (PAR = HR × RAP/MAP) | ratio | <10.0=0; 10.1–15.0=1; 15.1–20.0=2; 20.1–30.0=3; >30.0=4 | 0–4 |
| Hematologic | Platelet count (×10³/µL) | ×10³/µL | >120=0; 81–120=1; 51–80=2; 21–50=3; ≤20=4 | 0–4 |
| Neurologic | GCS | score | 15=0; 13–14=1; 10–12=2; 7–9=3; ≤6=4 | 0–4 |

**Formula:** `MODS = Respiratory(0-4) + Renal(0-4) + Hepatic(0-4) + Cardiovascular(0-4) + Hematologic(0-4) + Neurologic(0-4)`

**Score Range:** 0–24

**Interpretation:**

- **0:** No organ dysfunction
- **1–6:** Mild organ dysfunction
- **7–12:** Moderate dysfunction; increasing mortality
- **13–24:** Severe multi-organ dysfunction; very high mortality

**Reference:** Marshall JC, Cook DJ, Christou NV, et al. Multiple Organ Dysfunction Score: a reliable descriptor of a complex clinical outcome. Crit Care Med. 1995;23(10):1638-1652. PMID: 7587228

**Limitations:** Uses PAR (pressure-adjusted heart rate) which requires CVP measurement — not always available. Not designed for mortality prediction (descriptive). Superseded by SOFA in clinical practice. Single-center derivation.

