## Mortality Probability Model at ICU Admission (MPM₀)

**Purpose:** Predicts hospital mortality at ICU admission using data collected at the time of ICU admission (not 24 hours).

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Logit | Computed from the following variables | n/a | see below | see formula |

**Formula:** `MPM₀: Logit = −5.5291 + 0.8998(logit_coma/stupor) + 0.6098(logit_emergency) + 0.5775(logit_cancer) + 1.4024(logit_CPR_24h) + 0.9639(logit_chronic_renal) + 1.0905(logit_ICU_after_surgery) + 0.5172(logit_medical) + 0.1158(logit_heart_rate) + 0.0458(logit_systolic_BP) − 0.0299(logit_temperature) + 0.9637(logit_respiratory_support) + 0.6929(logit_cerebrovascular_disease). Predicted mortality = 1/(1 + e^(-logit)).`

**Score Range:** 0–100% predicted hospital mortality

**Interpretation:**

- **<5%:** Low predicted mortality
- **5–20%:** Moderate predicted mortality
- **20–50%:** High predicted mortality
- **>50%:** Very high predicted mortality

**Reference:** Lemeshow S, Teres D, Klar J, et al. Mortality Probability Models (MPM II) based on an international cohort of intensive care unit patients. JAMA. 1993;270(20):2478-2486. PMID: 8230626

**Limitations:** Calibrated to 1990s data. MPM₀-III updated but less widely used. Requires assessment at ICU admission time — cannot be used at 24h. Some variables are binary (less granular than APACHE/SAPS).

