## Rapid Emergency Medicine Score (REMS)

**Purpose:** Predicts in-hospital mortality for patients admitted from the emergency department using readily available physiological variables.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Age | Age in years | years | <45=0; 45–54=1; 55–64=2; 65–74=3; 75–84=4; ≥85=5 | 0–5 |
| Heart rate | Heart rate (bpm) | bpm | <70 or >109=2; 70–109=0 | 0–2 |
| Respiratory rate | RR (breaths/min) | breaths/min | <12 or >29=4; 12–29=0 | 0–4 |
| Systolic BP | SBP (mmHg) | mmHg | <70=4; 70–89=2; 90–129=0; 130–149=1; 150–179=2; ≥180=3 | 0–4 |
| SpO₂ | Oxygen saturation (%) | % | <75=4; 75–85=3; 86–89=2; ≥90=0 | 0–4 |
| GCS | Glasgow Coma Scale | score | 14–15=0; 8–13=2; ≤7=5 | 0–5 |

**Formula:** `REMS = Age + HR + RR + SBP + SpO₂ + GCS`

**Score Range:** 0–26

**Interpretation:**

- **0–4:** Low mortality risk (~1%)
- **5–8:** Moderate risk (~5%)
- **9–12:** High risk (~15%)
- **≥13:** Very high mortality risk (>30%)

**Reference:** Olsson T, Terent A, Lind L. Rapid Emergency Medicine Score: a new severity of illness score for the emergency department. Acad Emerg Med. 2004;11(2):131-137. PMID: 14759952

**Limitations:** Derived from Swedish single-center data. Not designed specifically for ICU. Superseded in some settings by NEWS2. Validated primarily in European populations.

---

## Modified Early Warning Score (MEWS)

**Purpose:** Identifies general ward patients at risk of clinical deterioration who may require ICU transfer, cardiac arrest, or death.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Respiratory rate | Breaths per minute | breaths/min | <9=1; 9–14=0; 15–20=1; 21–29=2; ≥30=3 | 0–3 |
| Heart rate | Beats per minute | bpm | <40=2; 41–50=1; 51–100=0; 101–110=1; 111–129=2; ≥130=3 | 0–3 |
| Systolic BP | mmHg | mmHg | <70=3; 71–80=2; 81–100=1; 101–199=0; ≥200=2 | 0–3 |
| Temperature | Core temperature (°C) | °C | <35=2; 35–38.4=0; ≥38.5=2 | 0–2 |
| AVPU / Consciousness | Alert, Voice, Pain, Unresponsive (or use GCS <14) | categorical | A=0; V/P/U=3 | 0–3 |

**Formula:** `MEWS = Respiratory_rate + Heart_rate + SBP + Temperature + Consciousness`

**Score Range:** 0–14+

**Interpretation:**

- **0–2:** Low risk of deterioration
- **3–4:** Increased risk — increase monitoring frequency, consider physician review
- **≥5:** High risk — urgent physician assessment, consider ICU transfer

**Reference:** Subbe CP, Kruger M, Rutherford P, Gemmel L. Validation of a modified Early Warning Score in medical admissions. QJM. 2001;94(10):521-526. PMID: 11588210

**Limitations:** Single-center validation (subsequent multi-center validations). Superseded in many settings by NEWS/NEWS2. AVPU is less granular than GCS. Not validated in all patient populations. Different thresholds used by different institutions.

