## National Early Warning Score 2 (NEWS2)

**Purpose:** Standardized track-and-trigger system to detect clinical deterioration in acutely ill adult patients using six physiological parameters.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Respiration rate | Breaths per minute | breaths/min | ≤8=3; 9–11=1; 12–20=0; 21–24=2; ≥25=3 | 0–3 |
| SpO₂ Scale 1 | Oxygen saturation (%) — use Scale 1 unless patient has confirmed hypercapnic respiratory failure | % | ≤91=3; 92–93=2; 94–95=1; ≥96=0 | 0–3 |
| SpO₂ Scale 2 (hypercapnic) | SpO₂ for patients with confirmed hypercapnic respiratory failure (target 88–92%) | % | ≤83 or >97=3; 84–85=2; 86–87=1; 88–92=0 (target); 93–94=1; 95–96=2 | 0–3 |
| Air or oxygen | Supplemental oxygen use | categorical | Air=0; Oxygen=2 | 0 or 2 |
| Temperature | Core temperature (°C) | °C | ≤35.0=3; 35.1–36.0=1; 36.1–38.0=0; 38.1–39.0=1; ≥39.1=2 | 0–3 |
| Systolic BP | Systolic blood pressure (mmHg) | mmHg | ≤90=3; 91–100=2; 101–110=1; 111–219=0; ≥220=3 | 0–3 |
| Heart rate | Pulse rate (bpm) | bpm | ≤40=3; 41–50=1; 51–90=0; 91–110=1; 111–130=2; ≥131=3 | 0–3 |
| Consciousness | AVPU or GCS | categorical | Alert=0; CVPU (Confusion/Voice/Pain/Unresponsive)=3 | 0 or 3 |

**Formula:** `NEWS2 = Respiratory + SpO₂(Scale1 or Scale2) + Air_or_O₂ + Temperature + SBP + HR + Consciousness. Aggregate score: if any single parameter scores 3, the aggregate score is automatically ≥3 (single-parameter trigger).`

**Score Range:** 0–20

**Interpretation:**

- **0:** Low clinical risk; routine monitoring
- **1–4 (low aggregate):** Low risk; consider assessment by ward nurse, increase monitoring frequency
- **3 in any single parameter:** Urgent assessment by ward nurse, inform medical team
- **5–6 (medium aggregate):** Key threshold — urgent review by clinician with competency in acute illness assessment
- **≥7:** Emergency response — urgent assessment by clinical team, consider ICU transfer

**Reference:** Royal College of Physicians. National Early Warning Score (NEWS) 2: Standardising the assessment of acute-illness severity in the NHS. Updated report of a working party. London: RCP, 2017. PMID: 28944504

**Limitations:** Validated primarily in UK NHS settings. Requires staff education and adherence. SpO₂ Scale 2 (hypercapnic patients) is less widely validated than Scale 1. Frequency of vital sign monitoring affects detection. Not validated for pediatric or obstetric patients.

