## Intensive Care Delirium Screening Checklist (ICDSC)

**Purpose:** Validated screening tool for delirium in ICU patients using eight items assessed over an 8-hour nursing shift.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Altered level of consciousness | A (alert), V (voice), P (pain), U (unresponsive), C (combative), S (sedated). A = 0; other = consider scoring | categorical | 0 or 1 | 0 or 1 |
| Inattention | Difficulty following commands or conversation | boolean | Yes/No | 0 or 1 |
| Disorientation | Incorrect response to questions about location, date, or identity | boolean | Yes/No | 0 or 1 |
| Hallucination-delusion psychosis | Presence of hallucinations, delusions, or psychotic behavior | boolean | Yes/No | 0 or 1 |
| Psychomotor agitation or retardation | Hyperactivity requiring sedation or hypoactivity with sluggish responses | boolean | Yes/No | 0 or 1 |
| Inappropriate speech or mood | Inappropriate content of speech or affect | boolean | Yes/No | 0 or 1 |
| Sleep-wake cycle disturbance | Sleeping ≤4 hours at night or sleeping ≥4 hours during the day | boolean | Yes/No | 0 or 1 |
| Symptom fluctuation | Fluctuation of any of the above items over 24 hours | boolean | Yes/No | 0 or 1 |

**Formula:** `ICDSC = Sum of all 8 items (0 or 1 each)`

**Score Range:** 0–8

**Interpretation:**

- **0–3:** Delirium not detected (below threshold)
- **4–8:** Delirium present (ICDSC ≥4 has sensitivity ~99%, specificity ~64%)

**Reference:** Bergeron N, Dubois MJ, Dumont M, et al. Intensive Care Delirium Screening Checklist: evaluation of a new screening tool. Intensive Care Med. 2001;27(5):859-864. PMID: 11430542

**Limitations:** Lower specificity than CAM-ICU (more false positives). Requires nursing observation over a shift. Does not distinguish delirium subtypes (hyperactive vs hypoactive). Some items are subjective.

