## Pneumonia Severity Index / PORT Score (PSI / PORT)

**Purpose:** Predicts 30-day mortality in community-acquired pneumonia patients to guide admission vs outpatient management decisions.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Age (males: age in years; females: age − 10) | Age in years; for females subtract 10 | years | continuous | age (or age − 10 for females) |
| Nursing home resident | Residing in a long-term care facility | boolean | Yes/No | +10 |
| Neoplastic disease | Active cancer | boolean | Yes/No | +30 |
| Liver disease | Chronic liver disease | boolean | Yes/No | +20 |
| Congestive heart failure | History of CHF | boolean | Yes/No | +10 |
| Cerebrovascular disease | History of stroke/TIA | boolean | Yes/No | +10 |
| Renal disease | Chronic renal insufficiency | boolean | Yes/No | +10 |
| Altered mental status | Confusion, disorientation | boolean | Yes/No | +20 |
| Pulse ≥125 bpm | Heart rate ≥125 | boolean | Yes/No | +10 |
| Respiratory rate ≥30 | RR ≥30/min | boolean | Yes/No | +20 |
| Systolic BP <90 mmHg | SBP <90 | boolean | Yes/No | +20 |
| Temperature <35°C or ≥40°C | Extreme temperature | boolean | Yes/No | +15 |
| pH <7.35 | Arterial pH below 7.35 | boolean | Yes/No | +30 |
| BUN ≥30 mg/dL (11 mmol/L) | Elevated blood urea nitrogen | boolean | Yes/No | +20 |
| Sodium <130 mEq/L | Hyponatremia | boolean | Yes/No | +20 |
| Glucose ≥250 mg/dL | Hyperglycemia | boolean | Yes/No | +10 |
| Hematocrit <30% | Anemia | boolean | Yes/No | +10 |
| PaO₂ <60 mmHg or SpO₂ <90% | Hypoxemia | boolean | Yes/No | +10 |
| Pleural effusion | Effusion on CXR | boolean | Yes/No | +10 |

**Formula:** `PSI = Age(males) or Age−10(females) + Nursing_home(10) + Cancer(30) + Liver(20) + CHF(10) + CVD(10) + Renal(10) + Altered_MS(20) + HR≥125(10) + RR≥30(20) + SBP<90(20) + Temp_extreme(15) + pH<7.35(30) + BUN≥30(20) + Na<130(20) + Glucose≥250(10) + Hct<30(10) + Hypoxemia(10) + Effusion(10)`

**Score Range:** 0–300+

**Interpretation:**

- **≤50 (Class I):** Low risk: 30-day mortality ~0.1%. Outpatient treatment.
- **51–70 (Class II):** Low risk: mortality ~0.6%. Outpatient treatment.
- **71–90 (Class III):** Low-moderate risk: mortality ~2.8%. Consider brief observation or outpatient.
- **91–130 (Class IV):** Moderate risk: mortality ~8.2%. Consider hospital admission.
- **>130 (Class V):** High risk: mortality ~29.2%. Hospital admission, consider ICU.

**Reference:** Fine MJ, Auble TE, Yealy DM, et al. A prediction rule to identify low-risk patients with community-acquired pneumonia. N Engl J Med. 1997;336(4):243-250. PMID: 8995086

**Limitations:** Complex (20 variables). Requires ABG for PaO₂. Age dominates the score (most young patients are Class I–III). Does not capture aspiration risk, MRSA risk, or immunocompromised status. Designed for CAP only (not HCAP, HAP, VAP). PSI Class I-II is particularly useful to identify low-risk patients.

---

## Confusion, Urea, Respiratory Rate, Blood Pressure, Age ≥65 Score (CURB-65)

**Purpose:** Simplified bedside score for assessing pneumonia severity and guiding site-of-care decisions in community-acquired pneumonia.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Confusion | New-onset confusion (abbreviated mental test score ≤8 or equivalent) | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Urea >7 mmol/L (>20 mg/dL) | Elevated blood urea nitrogen | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Respiratory rate ≥30/min | Tachypnea | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Blood pressure (SBP <90 or DBP ≤60) | Hypotension | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Age ≥65 years | Age | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |

**Formula:** `CURB-65 = Confusion(1) + Urea>7mmol/L(1) + RR≥30(1) + BP_hypotension(1) + Age≥65(1)`

**Score Range:** 0–5

**Interpretation:**

- **0–1:** Low mortality risk (~1–3%). Consider outpatient treatment.
- **2:** Moderate risk (~9%). Consider short inpatient or supervised outpatient treatment.
- **3–5:** High risk (~15–40%). Hospital admission; score 4–5 consider ICU.

**Reference:** Lim WS, van der Eerden MM, Laing R, et al. Defining community acquired pneumonia severity on presentation to hospital: an international derivation and validation study. Thorax. 2003;58(5):377-382. PMID: 12728155

**Limitations:** Does not include oxygenation (use CRB-65 if BUN unavailable). Less granular than PSI. Does not capture comorbidities or nursing home status. Does not identify specific pathogens or risk factors for resistant organisms. Score 2 is a 'gray zone' for site-of-care.

---

## Confusion, Respiratory Rate, Blood Pressure, Age ≥65 Score (CRB-65)

**Purpose:** Simplified CURB-65 variant without blood urea nitrogen; for settings where laboratory testing is not immediately available.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Confusion | New-onset confusion | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Respiratory rate ≥30/min | Tachypnea | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Blood pressure (SBP <90 or DBP ≤60) | Hypotension | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Age ≥65 years | Age | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |

**Formula:** `CRB-65 = Confusion(1) + RR≥30(1) + BP_hypotension(1) + Age≥65(1)`

**Score Range:** 0–4

**Interpretation:**

- **0:** Low risk. Consider outpatient management.
- **1–2:** Moderate risk. Consider hospital assessment.
- **3–4:** High risk. Hospital admission, consider ICU.

**Reference:** Lim WS, van der Eerden MM, Laing R, et al. Thorax. 2003;58(5):377-382. PMID: 12728155 (published as part of the CURB-65 derivation)

**Limitations:** Does not include BUN (less physiological data than CURB-65). Best used in prehospital or resource-limited settings. Same limitations as CURB-65.

