## SMART-COP Score

**Purpose:** Predicts need for intensive respiratory or vasopressor support (IRVS) in community-acquired pneumonia patients within 24 hours of ED presentation.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Low systolic BP | SBP <90 mmHg (males) or <100 (females) | boolean | Yes/No | 2 |
| Multilobar CXR involvement | ≥2 lobes involved on chest X-ray | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Albumin <3.5 g/dL | Low serum albumin | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Respiratory rate ≥25/min (age <50) or ≥30/min (age ≥50) | Tachypnea by age-adjusted cutoff | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Tachycardia ≥125/min | Heart rate ≥125 | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Confusion (new-onset) | Altered mental status | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Low oxygenation | PaO₂ <70 mmHg or SpO₂ <93% (age <50); PaO₂ <60 or SpO₂ <90% (age ≥50); or PaO₂/FiO₂ <250 (any age) | boolean | Yes/No | 2 |
| Arterial pH <7.35 | Acidosis on ABG | boolean | Yes/No | 2 |

**Formula:** `SMART-COP = SBP(2) + Multilobar(1) + Albumin(1) + RR(1) + HR≥125(1) + Confusion(1) + Low_O₂(2) + pH<7.35(2)`

**Score Range:** 0–11

**Interpretation:**

- **0–2:** Low risk of needing IRVS (~5–10%). Standard ward care.
- **3–4:** Moderate risk (~15–20%). Close monitoring.
- **5–6:** High risk (~30–40%). Consider ICU/HDU.
- **≥7:** Very high risk (>50%). ICU admission recommended.

**Reference:** Charles PG, Wolfe R, Whitby M, et al. SMART-COP: a tool for predicting the need for intensive respiratory or vasopressor support in community-acquired pneumonia. Clin Infect Dis. 2008;47(3):375-384. PMID: 18558884

**Limitations:** Requires ABG (not always available). Validated primarily in Australia and UK. Does not include comorbidities or immunosuppression. Albumin may not be immediately available. Focused on predicting need for IRVS (not mortality).

---

## Body Mass Index, Obstruction, Dyspnea, Exercise Capacity Index (BODE Index)

**Purpose:** Multidimensional prognostic index predicting all-cause mortality and respiratory mortality in COPD patients.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| BMI | Body mass index (kg/m²) | kg/m² | >21=0; ≤21=1 | 0 or 1 |
| Obstruction (FEV₁) | Post-bronchodilator FEV₁ % predicted | % | ≥65%=0; 50–64%=1; 36–49%=2; ≤35%=3 | 0–3 |
| Dyspnea (mMRC) | Modified Medical Research Council dyspnea scale | categorical | mMRC 0=0; 1=1; 2=2; 3=3; 4=4 | 0–4 |
| Exercise capacity (6MWD) | 6-minute walk distance | meters | ≥350m=0; 250–349m=1; 150–249m=2; ≤149m=3 | 0–3 |

**Formula:** `BODE = BMI(0-1) + FEV1(0-3) + mMRC(0-4) + 6MWD(0-3)`

**Score Range:** 0–10

**Interpretation:**

- **0–2:** Low risk. 4-year survival ~80%
- **3–4:** Moderate risk. 4-year survival ~67%
- **5–6:** High risk. 4-year survival ~57%
- **7–10:** Very high risk. 4-year survival ~18%

**Reference:** Celli BR, Cote CG, Marin JM, et al. The body-mass index, airflow obstruction, dyspnea, and exercise capacity index in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. N Engl J Med. 2004;350(10):1005-1012. PMID: 14999112

**Limitations:** Requires 6-minute walk test (not always performed in routine clinical practice). Does not capture exacerbation frequency. FEV₁ alone may miss important phenotypes. BMI cutoff of ≤21 is relatively low. Does not include biomarkers.

