## COPD Assessment Test (CAT)

**Purpose:** Patient-completed questionnaire assessing COPD symptom burden and impact on daily life.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Cough | I never cough (0) to I cough all the time (5) | categorical | 0–5 | 0–5 |
| Phlegm | I have no phlegm in my chest (0) to My chest is full of phlegm (5) | categorical | 0–5 | 0–5 |
| Chest tightness | My chest does not feel tight (0) to My chest feels very tight (5) | categorical | 0–5 | 0–5 |
| Breathlessness walking up a hill | Not breathless (0) to Very breathless (5) | categorical | 0–5 | 0–5 |
| Activity limitation | Not limited (0) to Very limited (5) | categorical | 0–5 | 0–5 |
| Confidence leaving home | Not confident (0) to Very confident (5) — note: 5 = confident, so NOT confident = higher score | categorical | 0–5 | 0–5 |
| Sleep | No trouble sleeping (0) to Cannot sleep at all (5) | categorical | 0–5 | 0–5 |
| Energy | Lots of energy (0) to No energy at all (5) | categorical | 0–5 | 0–5 |

**Formula:** `CAT = Sum of 8 items (each scored 0–5)`

**Score Range:** 0–40

**Interpretation:**

- **<10:** Low symptom impact
- **10–20:** Medium symptom impact
- **21–30:** High symptom impact
- **>30:** Very high symptom impact

**Reference:** Jones PW, Harding G, Berry P, et al. Development and first validation of the COPD Assessment Test. Eur Respir J. 2009;34(3):648-654. PMID: 19720809

**Limitations:** Patient-reported (subjective). Does not capture exacerbation history or spirometric severity. Cultural/language differences may affect scoring. Not a diagnostic tool.

---

## Modified Medical Research Council Dyspnea Scale (mMRC)

**Purpose:** Grades breathlessness severity in patients with COPD and other chronic lung diseases.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Dyspnea grade | Patient-reported level of breathlessness during daily activities | categorical | Grade 0–4 | see scale |

**Formula:** `mMRC scale:
0 = Only breathless with strenuous exercise
1 = Short of breath when hurrying on level ground or walking up a slight hill
2 = Walks slower than people of same age due to breathlessness or stops for breath when walking at own pace
3 = Stops for breath after walking 100 yards or after a few minutes on level ground
4 = Too breathless to leave house or breathless when dressing/undressing`

**Score Range:** 0–4

**Interpretation:**

- **0–1:** Mild breathlessness. COPD impact considered low in GOLD assessment.
- **2:** Moderate breathlessness. Threshold for impact assessment in GOLD guidelines.
- **3–4:** Severe breathlessness. Significant functional limitation.

**Reference:** Bestall JC, Paul EA, Garrod R, et al. Usefulness of the Medical Research Council (MRC) dyspnoea scale as a measure of disability in patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. Thorax. 1999;54(7):581-586. PMID: 10377201

**Limitations:** Single-item scale — limited granularity. Patient-reported. Does not capture all aspects of disease burden. Correlates moderately with quality of life but does not replace comprehensive assessment.

