## DECAF Score

**Purpose:** Predicts in-hospital mortality in acute exacerbations of COPD using five readily available clinical variables.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Dyspnea (eMRCD 5a or 5b) | Extended MRC Dyspnea scale: 5a = dyspnea after washing/dressing; 5b = housebound due to breathlessness | categorical | eMRCD 1–4=0; 5a=1; 5b=2 | 0–2 |
| Eosinopenia (<0.05 × 10⁹/L) | Blood eosinophil count <50 cells/µL | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Consolidation | Radiographic consolidation on CXR | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Acidemia (pH <7.30) | Arterial pH <7.30 | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| atrial Fibrillation | AF on ECG or known AF | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |

**Formula:** `DECAF = Dyspnea(0-2) + Eosinopenia(1) + Consolidation(1) + Acidemia(1) + atrial_Fibrillation(1)`

**Score Range:** 0–6

**Interpretation:**

- **0–1:** Low risk of in-hospital death (~1%). Consider ward-level care.
- **2:** Moderate risk (~4%). Consider closer monitoring.
- **3–6:** High risk (~10–50%). Consider HDU/ICU, palliative care discussion.

**Reference:** Steer J, Gibson J, Bourke SC. The DECAF Score: predicting hospital mortality in exacerbations of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. Thorax. 2012;67(11):970-976. PMID: 22863759

**Limitations:** Validated primarily in UK. Requires ABG. eMRCD 5a vs 5b may be difficult to assess acutely. Eosinopenia cutoff is laboratory-dependent. Not validated for non-COPD breathlessness.

