## STOP-BANG Questionnaire

**Purpose:** Preoperative and general screening tool for obstructive sleep apnea in surgical and primary care populations.

**Input Variables:**

| Variable | Description | Unit | Range/Options | Points |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Snoring | Do you snore loudly? | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Tired | Do you feel tired or sleepy during the daytime? | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Observed apnea | Has anyone observed you stop breathing during sleep? | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Pressure (BP) | Do you have or are you being treated for high blood pressure? | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| BMI >35 kg/m² | Body mass index >35 | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Age >50 years | Age over 50 | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Neck circumference >40 cm | Neck circumference >16 inches (40 cm) | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |
| Male sex | Male sex | boolean | Yes/No | 1 |

**Formula:** `STOP-BANG = Snoring(1) + Tired(1) + Observed_apnea(1) + Pressure_Bp(1) + BMI>35(1) + Age>50(1) + Neck>40cm(1) + Male(1)`

**Score Range:** 0–8

**Interpretation:**

- **0–2:** Low risk of OSA (AHI <5 or moderate/severe OSA unlikely)
- **3–4:** Intermediate risk. Further evaluation recommended.
- **5–8:** High risk of moderate-to-severe OSA (AHI ≥15 likely). Sleep study recommended.

**Reference:** Chung F, Yegneswaran B, Liao P, et al. STOP questionnaire: a tool to screen patients for obstructive sleep apnea. Anesthesiology. 2008;108(5):812-821. PMID: 18431116

**Limitations:** High sensitivity but moderate specificity for moderate-severe OSA (many false positives). Not diagnostic — requires confirmatory sleep study. BMI cutoff of 35 is high (misses non-obese OSA). Self-reported symptoms may be unreliable. Primarily validated in surgical populations.

